{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts","id":242936,"title":"Changeling 2.0 Brainspew 2: Contracts","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-08-28T03:10:31-07:00","id":242936,"title":"Changeling 2.0 Brainspew 2: Contracts","content":"Right now, we're chattering over Contract structure. The way it looks, they're going to come in four flavors:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Universal Contracts</b></span><br /> <br /> This is a Contract. It has a single name. It does what it's supposed to do. It'll have a level, roughly equating to its cost in Experiences. So a level 4 &quot;Contract of Storms&quot; will cost four Experiences. It's level 4, because it does pretty intense things, more intense than a level 1, 2, or 3. But it's important to note that there's no 1, 2, or 3 required. We'll lay out some guidelines for roughly what each level should be able to do. Guidelines, though, since there are always fiddly bits.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Seeming Contracts </b></span><br /> <br /> Seeming Contracts will be very broad Contracts that have multiple flavors, by Seeming. When you purchase one for its level in Experiences (so a level 4 costs 4), you get your Seeming's manifestation of it. For an Experience each, you can unlock other Seemings. If your Seeming isn't represented on the Contract (most will have 5, not 6), then if you want that Contract, you have to pay the extra Experience to unlock a different Seeming's manifestation when you pick it up.<br /> <br /> So, spitballing. This is totally brainspew I plugged out in thirty seconds to give you an idea. Don't concern yourself with the specifics.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Contract of Strength (2 dots)</b></span><br /> Makes you strong!<br /> Ogre: You get a direct Strength boost. Bam. Favored Seeming for this one.<br /> Elemental: You can draw on an example of your element to use its Structure instead of your dice pool for feats of strength.<br /> Fairest: When someone makes you look bad, your next strength action gets their successes added to yours.<br /> Darkling: When taking an action when nobody sees you, add your Stealth to your Strength.<br /> Beast: Grow a Size. Gain a Strength. Gain a Stamina.<br /> Wizened: Too bad, so sad. If you want Contract of Strength, pay an extra Experience and take another Seeming's manifestation.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Court Contracts </span></b><br /> <br /> These are contracts unique to one angle of the Court. So if we're doing a Court based on the maiden/mother/crone trichotomy, you would have a Maiden Contract, a Mother Contract, and a Crone Contract to go along with your Maiden Mantle, Mother Mantle, and Crone Mantle. These are like Universal Contracts, but you need an appropriate Mantle to buy them.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Goblin Contracts</span></b><br /> <br /> Nobody really makes deals with goblins, do they?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":70,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","user":"MachineIV","date":".  Changing the Experience cost re: feedback. 08-28-2014, 07:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-28T03:29:51-07:00","id":242958,"title":"","content":"Seems like contracts will be very expensive by the current proposal. I mean, I get that you might need to do something to make up for not needing to buy intervening levels, but I think the cost as listed is a bit much, at least for Universal ones.<br /> <br /> Noting that I do realize there's a benefit to just being able to buy higher level stuff straight away, it still means to get a contract at each level for Unviersal, you're paying 2 + 3 + 4 + 5 + 6 = 20 experiences, which is pretty hefty overall. I'd think it'd work better if Universal ones were the same cost as Seeming, unless they automatically can do more than one thing.<br /> <br /> That said, I like the overall idea of how these work so far, and the idea of Seeming Contracts having those additional aspects for other seemings that you can then also purchase.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":1130,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","user":"falco1029","date":". 08-28-2014, 06:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-28T03:30:18-07:00","id":242960,"title":"","content":"I...I make deals with Goblins. D:","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I had a signature but now I don't but it won't let me leave this blank so yeah.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/199-yue","name":"Yue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar199_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-28T04:12:50-07:00","id":242969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts?p=242958#post242958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seems like contracts will be very expensive by the current proposal. I mean, I get that you might need to do something to make up for not needing to buy intervening levels, but I think the cost as listed is a bit much, at least for Universal ones.<br /> <br /> Noting that I do realize there's a benefit to just being able to buy higher level stuff straight away, it still means to get a contract at each level for Unviersal, you're paying 2 + 3 + 4 + 5 + 6 = 20 experiences, which is pretty hefty overall. I'd think it'd work better if Universal ones were the same cost as Seeming, unless they automatically can do more than one thing.<br /> <br /> That said, I like the overall idea of how these work so far, and the idea of Seeming Contracts having those additional aspects for other seemings that you can then also purchase.</div> </div> </div> </div>I might make them flat dot cost. So 1, 2, 3, 4, 5. So, 15. That's the price of a Clan Discipline in Vampire 2.0. I'm not opposed to the idea.<br /> <br /> Edit: That said, I do want to decouple the idea that you need to buy them progressively. So the comparison's not exactly ideal. And I do think any given one will be a little more versatile than your average Vampire Discipline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-28T04:21:31-07:00","id":242972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts?p=242969#post242969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I might make them flat dot cost. So 1, 2, 3, 4, 5. So, 15. That's the price of a Clan Discipline in Vampire 2.0. I'm not opposed to the idea.<br /> <br /> Edit: That said, I do want to decouple the idea that you need to buy them progressively. So the comparison's not exactly ideal. And I do think any given one will be a little more versatile than your average Vampire Discipline.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, well, as I said, I do recognize the benefit of not needing to buy progressively, but either way I think making Universal the same level=cost would be better, myself. Either that, or addon a little something, maybe make it so instead of the old concept of a catch giving you a cost break, doing a Universal contract a specific way adds on an additional effect or something, that's a bit more potent than might otherwise be possible at that dot level? Or something in a similar vein.<br /> <br /> EDIT: For instance, using an existing example, Murkblur, if you swallow the eye of an animal, instead of having a cheaper cost, the blindness might affect an area or a number of targets equal to Wyrd, etc.<br /> <br /> Not that I'm suggesting catches themselves need to be done away with, I dunno what your plan is there, it was just a random thought, and meant to only be for Universals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":1130,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","user":"falco1029","date":". 08-28-2014, 07:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-28T04:33:39-07:00","id":242977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts?p=242972#post242972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Right, well, as I said, I do recognize the benefit of not needing to buy progressively, but either way I think making Universal the same level=cost would be better, myself. Either that, or addon a little something, maybe make it so instead of the old concept of a catch giving you a cost break, doing a Universal contract a specific way adds on an additional effect or something, that's a bit more potent than might otherwise be possible at that dot level? Or something in a similar vein.<br /> <br /> EDIT: For instance, using an existing example, Murkblur, if you swallow the eye of an animal, instead of having a cheaper cost, the blindness might affect an area or a number of targets equal to Wyrd, etc.<br /> <br /> Not that I'm suggesting catches themselves need to be done away with, I dunno what your plan is there, it was just a random thought, and meant to only be for Universals.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Catches are going to be pretty badass. They'll still exist, and basically in the same form. But we're going to focus on making them all matter. <br /> <br /> My initial apprehension about flat level was Contracts that only cost 1 Experience. But, I'm actually okay with that. Little cantrippy things, whatever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-28T04:34:43-07:00","id":242979,"title":"","content":"And, changed the post to reflect that point change. I dig.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-28T04:48:57-07:00","id":243004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts?p=242977#post242977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Catches are going to be pretty badass. They'll still exist, and basically in the same form. But we're going to focus on making them all matter.<br /> <br /> My initial apprehension about flat level was Contracts that only cost 1 Experience. But, I'm actually okay with that. Little cantrippy things, whatever.</div> </div> </div> </div>Works for me. The wording seems to imply contract creation guidelines, and that has me wondering; will it be easier in 2e to create a Contract from scratch, compared to the guide in Equinox Roads? Will it be expected Changelings might be coming up with their own little tricks that aren't in the core list, so guidelines will be given for that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-28T05:24:10-07:00","id":243019,"title":"","content":"Ooo, I love that example contract. Especially Fairest. You finally win a social exchange against me? Win it good? You're going out the motherfucking window, bitch! ^^","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-28T05:31:03-07:00","id":243022,"title":"","content":"What does it mean for a Seeming to be favored? <br /> <br /> Court Contracts: so you\u2019re now using \u201cCourt\u201d to mean \u201ca system of Courts\u201d in 1e\u2019s parlance? That is, you no longer have a Summer Court, but rather a Summer Mantle for the Seasonal Court? And Each Mantle gets a single Contract, which <i>cannot</i> be acquired without the Mantle? <br /> <br /> Goblin Contracts: Universal Contracts mostly replace these, save only for the activation costs \u2014 and it sounds like your planned revision for Catches will cover much of that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-28T05:42:57-07:00","id":243026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts?p=243022#post243022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Goblin Contracts: Universal Contracts mostly replace these, save only for the activation costs \u2014 and it sounds like your planned revision for Catches will cover much of that.</div> </div> </div> </div>It'd be cool for them to be experience cost free, but just things you can acquire during the game, the deal itself being the cost factor.<br /> <br /> How do these new Contracts work with a Changeling who has No Seeming? Do they always have to pay an extra experience to pick another Seeming? (Harsh!) Can they just pick whatever Seeming they want on a case-by-case basis for each Contract they learn? (OP!)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-28T05:45:57-07:00","id":243029,"title":"","content":"I'd prefer (Universal) Contracts to be layered, with multiple Clauses. Moving towards the model where a Contract does one thing and costs X amount seems way too straight forward for what are essentially deals made between the Fae and facets of reality. Since when did the Gentry become so direct?<br /> <br /> As a twist from 1st edition though, when Lost 'sign up' to a Contract they don't just get the first clause - they sign up to everything. Purchasing the Contract gives them access to every level of the power (1 to 5) but they have to be careful of the fine print, and can only safely use clauses they have 'initialed' (by purchasing with Experiences).<br /> <br /> The Contract itself lets them invoke the higher clauses but doing so comes with an increasingly steep surcharge (as they have to satisfy the Contract's penalty clauses), depending on the difference between the level they have purchased to and the level of the power used. One or two levels higher have a smallish (but still significant) cost, whereas invoking the highest levels when you don't have the right involves a huge (possibly game-changing?) cost to the character, such as having a very one-sided pledge forced upon you, or extending an invitation to your Keeper to come get you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-28T05:48:44-07:00","id":243032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts?p=243029#post243029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd prefer (Universal) Contracts to be layered, with multiple Clauses. Moving towards the model where a Contract does one thing and costs X amount seems way too straight forward for what are essentially deals made between the Fae and facets of reality. Since when did the Gentry become so direct?<br /> <br /> As a twist from 1st edition though, when Lost 'sign up' to a Contract they don't just get the first clause - they sign up to everything. Purchasing the Contract gives them access to every level of the power (1 to 5) but they have to be careful of the fine print, and can only safely use clauses they have 'initialed' (by purchasing with Experiences).<br /> <br /> The Contract itself lets them invoke the higher clauses but doing so comes with an increasingly steep surcharge (as they have to satisfy the Contract's penalty clauses), depending on the difference between the level they have purchased to and the level of the power used. One or two levels higher have a smallish (but still significant) cost, whereas invoking the highest levels when you don't have the right involves a huge (possibly game-changing?) cost to the character, such as having a very one-sided pledge forced upon you, or extending an invitation to your Keeper to come get you.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see it as the opposite really. Structured 1 to 5 contracts seem too 'direct' and predictable, as if every facet of reality has a number of things it can do divisible by 5? THAT makes no sense for Fae, to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-28T06:17:56-07:00","id":243048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts?p=243022#post243022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What does it mean for a Seeming to be favored?<br /> <br /> Court Contracts: so you\u2019re now using \u201cCourt\u201d to mean \u201ca system of Courts\u201d in 1e\u2019s parlance? That is, you no longer have a Summer Court, but rather a Summer Mantle for the Seasonal Court? And Each Mantle gets a single Contract, which <i>cannot</i> be acquired without the Mantle?<br /> <br /> Goblin Contracts: Universal Contracts mostly replace these, save only for the activation costs \u2014 and it sounds like your planned revision for Catches will cover much of that.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Favored, in this case, is just a spitball thing. Basically, any given Seeming Contract is favored by one Seeming. So its manifestation is going to be a little more generally useful; that Seeming will have a sort of 'elemental essence' of that Contract. <br /> <br /> Er. A Court System is a Court System. I don't know if we have the word for that yet. But I don't want to talk too much about it, because it's a really fundamental thing that'll go left field if I start into it too much here. If you have Seasonal Courts, you'll still have Summer, Winter, et cetera. I think we'll use a Mantle system and a Court Goodwill system. If you have Goodwill, you can get Court Contracts. Again, super early. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-28T06:19:42-07:00","id":243050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts?p=243004#post243004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Works for me. The wording seems to imply contract creation guidelines, and that has me wondering; will it be easier in 2e to create a Contract from scratch, compared to the guide in Equinox Roads? Will it be expected Changelings might be coming up with their own little tricks that aren't in the core list, so guidelines will be given for that?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> We'll be giving guidelines for building them. Truth be told, it's been a long time since I've read that part of Equinox Road, so I can't speak to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-28T06:36:04-07:00","id":243058,"title":"","content":"This sounds interesting but aren't they a bit more expensive than they currently are. If they are more powerful I could understand the boost in price. I hope this will alleviate some of the issues I have with a number of contracts. What are you plans for hearth if I might ask? Also if you have no seeming do you simply pay a normal cost or does everything count as unfavored?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-28T06:38:23-07:00","id":243062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Unahim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts?p=243026#post243026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It'd be cool for them to be experience cost free, but just things you can acquire during the game, the deal itself being the cost factor.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seconding this notion. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Unahim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts?p=243026#post243026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do these new Contracts work with a Changeling who has No Seeming? Do they always have to pay an extra experience to pick another Seeming? (Harsh!) Can they just pick whatever Seeming they want on a case-by-case basis for each Contract they learn? (OP!)</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019d go with the former: harsh; but it goes with the fact that you never really achieved agency.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-28T06:44:26-07:00","id":243065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts?p=243048#post243048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Favored, in this case, is just a spitball thing. Basically, any given Seeming Contract is favored by one Seeming. So its manifestation is going to be a little more generally useful; that Seeming will have a sort of 'elemental essence' of that Contract.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm\u2026 maybe this should be phrased in two parts: the first part of the Favored Seeming\u2019s manifestation of the Contract can be acquired by other Seemings if they pay the extra Experience; the second part of it is only available to the Favored Seeming, and generally acts as an enhancement to or extrapolation of the first part.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-28T06:45:29-07:00","id":243066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts?p=243050#post243050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> We'll be giving guidelines for building them. Truth be told, it's been a long time since I've read that part of Equinox Road, so I can't speak to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The basics come down to it's very very difficult, and honestly I only remember parts of it, myself. It involves making an oath with the aspect itself, performing a fairly heft major endeavor, and then a few more difficult steps I forget that solidify it as a contract (before then it ends up being a goblin contract of sacrifice, essentially), and I know there's a lot of willpower expenditure involved, if I recall.<br /> <br /> Basically, I'd be happy if it was easier than that :P<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-28T06:46:21-07:00","id":243067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts?p=243062#post243062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seconding this notion.<br /> <br /> I\u2019d go with the former: harsh; but it goes with the fact that you never really achieved agency.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh. I disagree. In terms of abilities they should be jack of all trades. They don't Favor anything but they don't Unfavor things. It should count everything unfavored. It should be, in mage terms, having all arcana at common rather than ruling or inferior.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-28T08:05:45-07:00","id":243098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts?p=243058#post243058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This sounds interesting but aren't they a bit more expensive than they currently are. If they are more powerful I could understand the boost in price. I hope this will alleviate some of the issues I have with a number of contracts. What are you plans for hearth if I might ask? Also if you have no seeming do you simply pay a normal cost or does everything count as unfavored?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If you don't have a Seeming, I think everything would be unfavored. Unless we decide to do Seeming-Free Contracts. I doubt that'll happen. The point break really should be a perk that comes along with the agency grab that Seemings reflect. If you didn't grab agency, you're less able to take charge later. <br /> <br /> By and large, I do expect a bit of a power boost around the board. Look to Blood &amp; Smoke/Requiem 2e for an idea of the shift there.<br /> <br /> I don't have plans for any specific Contracts yet. The idea is, I'll figure out the format (which is what I'm doing here), then I'll work up a creation system (I'll probably do that myself) then let the authors handle individual Contracts as they see fit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-28T08:08:00-07:00","id":243103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts?p=243065#post243065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm\u2026 maybe this should be phrased in two parts: the first part of the Favored Seeming\u2019s manifestation of the Contract can be acquired by other Seemings if they pay the extra Experience; the second part of it is only available to the Favored Seeming, and generally acts as an enhancement to or extrapolation of the first part.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I kind of like that idea, but I'd have to see if it's something my writers find feasible for every Seeming Contract.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-28T08:09:15-07:00","id":243104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts?p=243066#post243066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The basics come down to it's very very difficult, and honestly I only remember parts of it, myself. It involves making an oath with the aspect itself, performing a fairly heft major endeavor, and then a few more difficult steps I forget that solidify it as a contract (before then it ends up being a goblin contract of sacrifice, essentially), and I know there's a lot of willpower expenditure involved, if I recall.<br /> <br /> Basically, I'd be happy if it was easier than that :P<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah... That's prohibitive. I don't really enjoy a lot of prohibitive stuff at the table. So it's liable to be significantly easier than that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-28T08:20:13-07:00","id":243136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts?p=243098#post243098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> If you don't have a Seeming, I think everything would be unfavored. Unless we decide to do Seeming-Free Contracts. I doubt that'll happen. The point break really should be a perk that comes along with the agency grab that Seemings reflect. If you didn't grab agency, you're less able to take charge later.<br /> <br /> By and large, I do expect a bit of a power boost around the board. Look to Blood &amp; Smoke/Requiem 2e for an idea of the shift there.<br /> <br /> I don't have plans for any specific Contracts yet. The idea is, I'll figure out the format (which is what I'm doing here), then I'll work up a creation system (I'll probably do that myself) then let the authors handle individual Contracts as they see fit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh. If that's the case what do they get as a bonus if it's still a merit. What's essentially one clarity for all drawbacks seems really off.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-28T08:22:54-07:00","id":243139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts#post242936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right now, we're chattering over Contract structure. The way it looks, they're going to come in four flavors:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Universal Contracts</b></span><br /> <br /> This is a Contract. It has a single name. It does what it's supposed to do. It'll have a level, roughly equating to its cost in Experiences. So a level 4 &quot;Contract of Storms&quot; will cost four Experiences. It's level 4, because it does pretty intense things, more intense than a level 1, 2, or 3. But it's important to note that there's no 1, 2, or 3 required. We'll lay out some guidelines for roughly what each level should be able to do. Guidelines, though, since there are always fiddly bits.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Seeming Contracts </b></span><br /> <br /> Seeming Contracts will be very broad Contracts that have multiple flavors, by Seeming. When you purchase one for its level in Experiences (so a level 4 costs 4), you get your Seeming's manifestation of it. For an Experience each, you can unlock other Seemings. If your Seeming isn't represented on the Contract (most will have 5, not 6), then if you want that Contract, you have to pay the extra Experience to unlock a different Seeming's manifestation when you pick it up.<br /> <br /> [snip]<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Court Contracts </span></b><br /> <br /> These are contracts unique to one angle of the Court. So if we're doing a Court based on the maiden/mother/crone trichotomy, you would have a Maiden Contract, a Mother Contract, and a Crone Contract to go along with your Maiden Mantle, Mother Mantle, and Crone Mantle. These are like Universal Contracts, but you need an appropriate Mantle to buy them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hmm. So are the &quot;standard&quot; Contracts going to be Universal, as they are now, or are most of them going to be more collections of Contracts for each Seeming?<br /> <br /> I guess I'm wondering: are Seeming Contracts more analogous to current &quot;normal&quot; Contracts or Court Contracts?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Unahim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts?p=243026#post243026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It'd be cool for them to be experience cost free, but just things you can acquire during the game, the deal itself being the cost factor.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ooh, thirded. With the dot rating determining what they're &quot;equivalent&quot; to for trading. (And if you don't try to angle for a better deal, you can just pay the XP to do it offscreen without risking anything.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":877,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","user":"MugaSofer","date":". 08-28-2014, 11:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","name":"MugaSofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar877_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-28T08:28:42-07:00","id":243154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts?p=243104#post243104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yeah... That's prohibitive. I don't really enjoy a lot of prohibitive stuff at the table. So it's liable to be significantly easier than that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Brilliant.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Otherwise, I like the idea people are throwing around about Goblin Contracts being 'free' but paid for with IC costs. I'd love if some of the goblin vow merit's intent was woven into how Goblin Contracts themselves come about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-28T08:32:38-07:00","id":243157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Unahim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts?p=243026#post243026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It'd be cool for them to be experience cost free, but just things you can acquire during the game, the deal itself being the cost factor.</div> </div> </div> </div>And yeah. I like that. I'll see what my team feels on it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-28T10:11:02-07:00","id":243235,"title":"","content":"All in all I'd say that this addresses all my concerns from the first brainspew. I was worried that the Seeming mechaincs could be inflexible if you wanted a particular faerie tale power but had to find 5/6 spins on it to make a contract. Universal Contracts addresses that. I was also worried about the thematics of Seeming contracts. That was addressed long ago when I learned what Seemings actually represent in Changeling 2.0.<br /> <br /> Mind you - I am curious for how you'd do the talk to animals power as a Seeming Contract. (Snow White was definately a Fairest or no-Seeming who can talk to animals)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts?p=243048#post243048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Er. A Court System is a Court System. I don't know if we have the word for that yet. But I don't want to talk too much about it, because it's a really fundamental thing that'll go left field if I start into it too much here.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm very much looking forward to the Courts brainspew.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts?p=243029#post243029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd prefer (Universal) Contracts to be layered, with multiple Clauses.</div> </div> </div> </div> In practice; this isn't any different from having 4 or 5 different universal contracts that cover a similar subject.<br /> <br /> Take my all time favourite - Contract of Reflections. You could easily run that as five (well four, because I have no idea what the 5th dot is supposed to do) different universal contracts, I don't think that anything breaks if you can buy the clauses out of order.<br /> <br /> That said; I do think that it might be useful if a Contract could have perquisite contracts - summon animals could have talking to animals as a perquisite. Or a contract to spin magic spider-web could unlock useful abilities like detecting intruders on you web or. <br /> <br /> It just seems like something that might be useful if you want to create lots of related powers for a changeling with a very strong theme.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts?p=243029#post243029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Moving towards the model where a Contract does one thing and costs X amount seems way too straight forward for what are essentially deals made between the Fae and facets of reality. Since when did the Gentry become so direct?</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally. I like it.<br /> <br /> Firstly, who says that the Gentry created the Contracts? I like to think that Changelings created Contracts, and form that angle they work great. Contracts being straght forward represent what Changelings <u>want</u> their magic and their life to be. Straight forward and safe.<br /> <br /> However catches, and the fact many contracts have unpredictable effects (compare the old Stone 1 to Vigor), shows that Changelings haven't quite suceeeded in creating anything straight forward and safe. It's a strong image which I like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-28T10:31:11-07:00","id":243269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts#post242936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Seeming Contracts </b></span><br /> <br /> Seeming Contracts will be very broad Contracts that have multiple flavors, by Seeming. When you purchase one for its level in Experiences (so a level 4 costs 4), you get your Seeming's manifestation of it. For an Experience each, you can unlock other Seemings. If your Seeming isn't represented on the Contract (most will have 5, not 6), then if you want that Contract, you have to pay the extra Experience to unlock a different Seeming's manifestation when you pick it up.<br /> <br /> So, spitballing. This is totally brainspew I plugged out in thirty seconds to give you an idea. Don't concern yourself with the specifics.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Contract of Strength (2 dots)</b></span><br /> Makes you strong!<br /> Ogre: You get a direct Strength boost. Bam. Favored Seeming for this one.<br /> Elemental: You can draw on an example of your element to use its Structure instead of your dice pool for feats of strength.<br /> Fairest: When someone makes you look bad, your next strength action gets their successes added to yours.<br /> Darkling: When taking an action when nobody sees you, add your Stealth to your Strength.<br /> Beast: Grow a Size. Gain a Strength. Gain a Stamina.<br /> Wizened: Too bad, so sad. If you want Contract of Strength, pay an extra Experience and take another Seeming's manifestation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was opposed to the idea of Seeming-specific Contract manifestations, due to having had a lot of fun with &quot;nonstandard&quot; Contract loadouts, but this seems to support that even better. I approve!<br /> <br /> However, I'm wondering how taking out-of-Seeming variants will work during chargen, where resources are more restricted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-28T10:53:45-07:00","id":243281,"title":"","content":"Hmm. Gonna need some time to think on this on the whole, but as a quick thought:<br /> <br /> I know I bought Goblin Contracts, but I agree with the idea no one bought them. Still, it'd be a shame for some of that element to go, so as an idea: When you invoke a Catch for a Contract, can a Goblin aspect come in? My initial thought was perform a catch and fail the contract leads to a Dramatic Failure, but it could lead to some Paradox-esque Success sort of thing as well, though I'm less fond of the second idea.<br /> <br /> I dunno, food for thought.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-28T11:05:47-07:00","id":243289,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty fond of this setup as well, the seeming-specific effects are fun and reinforce the flavor of the seemings. On the other hand, I'm curious how this will play for character creation. This sort of bugged me with promethean too, where the ability to jump ahead in dots actually ended up giving starting characters less power (unless I was reading it wrong, which is entirely possible) because where most templates get at least three powers for starting with three dots, prometheans who want anything better than a one dot power would have to put two or three dots toward a single ability and come out with less by the end of it. I personally sort of liked the way changelings started with a deeper bag of tricks than everyone else (not counting mages, obviously), and ideally I'd like to see that represented in 2.0 as well. maybe do something similar to mage where you get a lot of dots to work with but limiting the power level of the contracts you can buy?<br /> <br /> As for goblin contracts, I always sort of liked them but I can see where they'd be a bit tricky to translate. The idea that they're free as long as you're willing to take the drawback is interesting but I'm not sure how well that would balance. Actually what might be a fun idea for them is that once you take it you have to perform the catch at least once a day even if you're not using the contract, that might be a good way to work it into the story and keep people from just piling up on &quot;free&quot; powers, or maybe work them kind of like promise tokens from rites of spring where you can do something impressive for free but the short term benefit gives someone or something else a permanent advantage over you, or some other sort of long-term price. I dunno, if it doesn't fit in I suppose it wouldn't be a huge loss to the game if you can't figure out a good system for it. plus if it doesn't show up in the core and you come up with something later it can go in a later book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/807-arcadianawakened","name":"ArcadianAwakened","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-28T11:22:51-07:00","id":243297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts?p=243157#post243157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And yeah. I like that. I'll see what my team feels on it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was just going to suggest a very similar setup for Goblin Contracts, so as to differentiate them from &quot;normal&quot; Contracts and making them a more attractive option.<br /> <br /> Either way, I would much like to see Goblin Contracts stay in the game, but perhaps as a wider category of bizarre and dangerous effects derived from the denizens of the Hedge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-28T11:38:50-07:00","id":243305,"title":"","content":"Instead of having Catches provide a cost break, which can be kinda lack-luster IMO, what about them instead amping up the effect of the Contract? <br /> <br /> For example: Say you have a contact that causes the target bad luck, a dramatic failure or something, with the Catch if the Changeling Catches them performing some traditionally bad luck action (Breaking a mirror, walking under a ladder, etc.). Instead of just getting to curse them for free, he could instead give them a really nasty, lasting curse that continues to haunt them. Mechanically this could be as simple as automatically getting an Exceptional Success.<br /> <br /> Heck, it could even be a set of options, if the catch is met the Changeling may choose one of the following: Wave all costs for using the contract, Automatically upgrade Success to Exceptional Success, ignore all penalties to the roll, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-28T12:03:09-07:00","id":243317,"title":"","content":"Catches working like Reach might work; with one of the options being getting it without Glamour.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-28T12:08:32-07:00","id":243321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts?p=243305#post243305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Heck, it could even be a set of options, if the catch is met the Changeling may choose one of the following: Wave all costs for using the contract, Automatically upgrade Success to Exceptional Success, ignore all penalties to the roll, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>I kinda like this. If appropriate, I can even see some Contracts having multiple Catches: the Changeling can select as many of the available options* at once as Catches they fulfill. Care would obviously need to be taken in setting this up, but there are possibilities here.<br /> <br /> * These options could vary by Contract. Perhaps with a standard set, some Contracts having their own options, some Contracts disabling certain options, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-28T12:08:41-07:00","id":243322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_poste