000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-28T12:11:51-07:00","id":243325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts?p=243322#post243322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">More options never hurts.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're going to regret saying that. Mwahahahahaha <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-28T14:24:37-07:00","id":243402,"title":"","content":"Pretty awesome looking, but, I'm not really someone who can comment much on mechanical stuff.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I do hope the Contracts are more powerful though, which seems to be the case.<br /> <br /> And... yeah, that's my two cents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-28T15:11:42-07:00","id":243449,"title":"","content":"Oh yes! One of my wishes for Contracts has come true! Oh joy!<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1996-firefly-night","name":"Firefly Night","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-28T15:46:18-07:00","id":243465,"title":"","content":"Going to start with:<br /> <br /> This format addresses the issues I had with the whole &quot;seeming specific aspects of Contracts&quot; in that other thread. So wholehearted thumbs up and kudos for addressing the problem within the context of what you want to do.<br /> <br /> The format looks good. Feels very grab-baggy. On the one hand, that fits Changeling. On the other hand, I feel pen and paper games like this benefit from a sense of progression. In this system if a Changeling who can conjure Tornados doesn't do so because they are the master of winds, a witch surviving from a living malestrom for a keeper and dedicating her life to the study of weather patterns. She can conjure Tornados because she paid 5 EXP, reached into the grab bag of Changeling Powers, and happened to pull out a Tornado that day. Joe Schmuckatelly, the hobo down the street of questionable mental acuity (and hygiene) could do the same thing next week because he feels like it.<br /> <br /> The easy solution to this is to have some Contracts have requirements, or to have a classication of &quot;Advanced Contracts&quot; that have requirements (see: Exploits). You can also use catches by doing things like &quot;This 5 Dot Contract is actually pretty lame, *unless* you fulfill its catch. Then it summons Tornados. P.S. Its Catch is actually an IC cost / sacrifice and its big and important.&quot; The idea being to make 4-5 Dot Contracts feel weighty or like the culmination of a journey rather than what magic token your going to buy today.<br /> <br /> Unless, of course, thats the entire idea. Maybe what you want is to make Changeling &quot;magic&quot; feel divorced from the character's skill level so it doesn't feel like its really <i>theirs</i>. If so then what you have is fine, although I'd make sure to point out that its functioning as intended in the text.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-28T16:04:07-07:00","id":243473,"title":"","content":"Oh hey. Two other things. <br /> <br /> 1) Is this a good place to talk about Catches, or is that a later discussion? I mention it because Goblin Contracts are sort of defined by their catches.<br /> <br /> 2) What are you thinking of for dicepools on these things? How about Clash of Wills? There is no immediately obvious option, though there are a few options with a bit of thinking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-28T18:15:43-07:00","id":243513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts?p=243473#post243473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh hey. Two other things.<br /> <br /> 1) Is this a good place to talk about Catches, or is that a later discussion? I mention it because Goblin Contracts are sort of defined by their catches.<br /> <br /> 2) What are you thinking of for dicepools on these things? How about Clash of Wills? There is no immediately obvious option, though there are a few options with a bit of thinking.</div> </div> </div> </div>1) Not yet. I want to have a separate discussion about that. <br /> <br /> 2) I haven't gotten that far in. I have some thoughts, but I haven't given them the second thought-over necessary before posting them and starting a divergent conversation. I'm definitely not thrilled with Attribute or Skill + Wyrd.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-28T19:52:30-07:00","id":243549,"title":"","content":"I would really rather prerequisites be kept to a minimum. One of my biggest gripes about <b>Exalted</b> is the elaborate Charm trees.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-28T20:06:14-07:00","id":243556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts?p=243549#post243549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would really rather prerequisites be kept to a minimum. One of my biggest gripes about <b>Exalted</b> is the elaborate Charm trees.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't think we'll have much in the way of prerequisites, beyond Mantle/Goodwill for Courts. I don't see any Contracts as requiring other Contracts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-28T23:10:03-07:00","id":243657,"title":"","content":"I don't have much to comment on with regards the mechanics. I alas have little imagination when it comes to crunch. It has to be seen in action for me to develop an opinion worth spit. <br /> <br /> That said, I did have a few thoughts left over from last edition that seemed appropriate to throw out. Food for thought.<br /> <br /> 1. I got the (vague) impression from the Changeling books, especially Equinox Road, that establishing a new courtly contract and especially crafting a new court system was a BIG deal that would profoundly effect the changeling who had done so. Could we perhaps explore in a bit more detail what happens to such fae? And for that matter, whatever happened to the courtly founders of the Seasons (or whichever Courts we are dealing with)? Are they still alive? Do they become True Fae? Remain &quot;mere&quot; changelings? Become...something stranger than either?<br /> <br /> 2. I never had a good grasp on what &quot;Making a Contract with an Aspect of Reality&quot; should look like in game. A little more concrete detail on what a Changeling might experience would be lovely (and if it varies from person to person, a few descriptive examples to choose from would be just as lovely). And do these aspects ever...play a part later in the story? Pop in for tea and a quick chat? Do others ever see these aspects, or is it solely the Changeling who holds the Contract? Do these &quot;Aspects&quot; ever have favors to ask or things to demand of the Fae? I could see a freehold in which certain fae from time to time serve as diplomats to the shadows of evening in the lakeside park or errand runners for that pack of stray dogs on 2nd street. <br /> <br /> 3. Going off that last idea, I remember a fairy tale in which a clever Jack of all trades captures Death in a magic sack. Everything is great until he realizes that people keep getting older and older and no one is dying. So he let's death out and he does his thing. So imagine an occasion when a shard of reality needs a bit of fae intervention to continue doing its job. That gust of wind needs a couple notes delivered to the old goblin witch in the Hedge before people in the city start having trouble breathing. You get the idea. We know full well how Contracts benefit the Fae. What do they do for Reality, exactly?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-29T06:41:16-07:00","id":243850,"title":"","content":"Question: Do you intend on &quot;Contracts on the Fly&quot; or &quot;Improvised Contracts&quot; to be a thing at all, in any form? Goblin Vows, etc etc. Do you intend on a &quot;Wyrd Sorcery&quot; system at all, similar to Blood Magic or Mage or what have you?<br /> <br /> Also, been thinking about dicepools. I also feel icky about Attribute/Skill + Wyrd, but I also feel that it <i>works</i> if not better idea can be had. I also can't think of a better dicepool at this moment.<br /> <br /> A quick trip into the potentially absurd: do we need dicepools at all? What if changelings buy success(s) or stages or effect or etc by spending more and more glamour or fulfilling catches or standing on their head. Whatever. Penalties are replaced with a surcharge on the cost.<br /> <br /> Alternative or perhaps synergistic with the above, what if Contracts are something you roll against instead of something that the Changeling rolls? If a Changeling has a contract that says they can pick up a truck. Then they pick up the truck. Period. No roll. If someone wants to contest that then they have to roll with some penalty.<br /> <br /> Just spitballing out of left field here. *shrugs*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1157,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","user":"SoulGambit","date":". 08-29-2014, 09:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-29T07:26:21-07:00","id":243906,"title":"","content":"So wait, are the Courts limited to one Contract per Court? Would you be doing away with the Fleeting and Eternal Season Contracts for example? I rather liked the Physical-Manifestation/Emotion-Association dichotomy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-29T17:56:02-07:00","id":244433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts?p=243906#post243906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So wait, are the Courts limited to one Contract per Court? Would you be doing away with the Fleeting and Eternal Season Contracts for example? I rather liked the Physical-Manifestation/Emotion-Association dichotomy.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not 100% sure yet. We're going to be fitting a lot of Courts into this book. I don't know that we'll have room to have twice or more than that number in additional Contracts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-29T18:08:49-07:00","id":244438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts?p=244433#post244433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Not 100% sure yet. We're going to be fitting a lot of Courts into this book. I don't know that we'll have room to have twice or more than that number in additional Contracts.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Which doesn't mean there isn't room for expansion later. I mean even the first edition did that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-29T18:42:45-07:00","id":244452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts?p=244433#post244433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Not 100% sure yet. We're going to be fitting a lot of Courts into this book. I don't know that we'll have room to have twice or more than that number in additional Contracts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh. That sucks. My favourite Contracts are the Seasonal Contracts and if I had to choose between the two flavors of them, I'd have to think long and hard about it. The Fleeting clauses wins, of course, but still. <br /> <br /> Can't win 'em all. Anyway, it is hard to get too upset given that I have no idea what the actual rules and stuff will be. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1996-firefly-night","name":"Firefly Night","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-29T20:12:33-07:00","id":244470,"title":"","content":"Perhaps instead, you could do them like seeming contracts--the contract itself is Fleeting (emotions) or Eternal (literal), which your court colors. However, the idea of more than the core four courts is awesome. Ive always been a fan of the celestial and directional courts, and losing some core contracts to get some for those would be awesome. When you say you're packing it with Courts.. Is that just the already existing 12? or are we finally getting to see some primal african and native american courts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-30T00:58:05-07:00","id":244659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts?p=244433#post244433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not 100% sure yet. We're going to be fitting a lot of Courts into this book. I don't know that we'll have room to have twice or more than that number in additional Contracts.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm holding my breath for the Courts brainspew here <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> That said, there is a fundamental difference between &quot;Courts only get one Contract each&quot; and &quot;There's only enough space to give each Courts one example Contract&quot;. I mean, there might be a Winter Masques 2.0 with room for additional Contracts for each corebook Court sometime after Changeling 2.0","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-30T05:25:16-07:00","id":244744,"title":"","content":"Is there a particular reason you have to have one power of each level in a Universal contract?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-30T05:28:38-07:00","id":244747,"title":"","content":"I'm under the impression you don't have to have one power of each level in any kind of Contract.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-30T05:33:38-07:00","id":244750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts?p=244747#post244747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm under the impression you don't have to have one power of each level in any kind of Contract.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, I meant design wise - do Universal Contracts <i>have</i> to be designed that each one has a level 1, level 2, level 3 and so on power. It seems that if you're having each power able to be bought nonsequentially you open open a lot off design space by loosening the 'standard' design concepts","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-30T07:01:01-07:00","id":244777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>That Other Guy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts?p=244750#post244750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sorry, I meant design wise - do Universal Contracts <i>have</i> to be designed that each one has a level 1, level 2, level 3 and so on power. It seems that if you're having each power able to be bought nonsequentially you open open a lot off design space by loosening the 'standard' design concepts</div> </div> </div> </div>No. There's no sequence. None at all. <br /> <br /> You might see Contract of Fog at 1, Contract of Wind at 2, Contract of Storms at 3, Contract of Lightning at 4, and Contract of Earthquake at 5. But that'd be coincidence. Each is its own animal. You don't need any of the others. They're not part of a &quot;weather suite&quot;. They're just different Contracts at different levels. No prerequisite Contracts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-30T10:29:02-07:00","id":244865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts?p=244659#post244659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm holding my breath for the Courts brainspew here <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> That said, there is a fundamental difference between &quot;Courts only get one Contract each&quot; and &quot;There's only enough space to give each Courts one example Contract&quot;. I mean, there might be a Winter Masques 2.0 with room for additional Contracts for each corebook Court sometime after Changeling 2.0</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That would be something we'd really love to do. It could be challenging with our Court format (we're offering examples by city), but I'd really like to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-30T10:54:51-07:00","id":244880,"title":"","content":"Am I the only one who thinks Eternal Autumn\u00b4s clauses were a bit... underpowered, except level 4 Riding of the Falling Leaves?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-30T14:07:25-07:00","id":244989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts?p=244433#post244433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Not 100% sure yet. We're going to be fitting a lot of Courts into this book. I don't know that we'll have room to have twice or more than that number in additional Contracts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmm.... I'm not sure how I feel about decreased core focus on the Seasonal Courts (all for strong supplement coverage!). The evocation of Denial (Spring), Anger (Summer), Bargaining (Autumn), and Depression (Winter) is pretty central to the themes of trauma and survival.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-30T14:20:29-07:00","id":244993,"title":"","content":"Any hope of a Goblin Vow type mechanic making it into the core, where a character can exchange services with a force of nature for more free form effects?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-30T15:14:55-07:00","id":245015,"title":"","content":"maybe each kith should be able to goblin vow with whatever their kith is based on by default and you can buy other aspects as merits?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/807-arcadianawakened","name":"ArcadianAwakened","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-30T18:34:40-07:00","id":245117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts?p=244777#post244777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No. There's no sequence. None at all.<br /> <br /> You might see Contract of Fog at 1, Contract of Wind at 2, Contract of Storms at 3, Contract of Lightning at 4, and Contract of Earthquake at 5. But that'd be coincidence. Each is its own animal. You don't need any of the others. They're not part of a &quot;weather suite&quot;. They're just different Contracts at different levels. No prerequisite Contracts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nice!<br /> <br /> ...now, I'm REALLY curious what the Contact of Fang and Talon looks like, assuming it's still a part of the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-30T19:05:16-07:00","id":245127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>That Other Guy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts?p=245117#post245117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nice!<br /> <br /> ...now, I'm REALLY curious what the Contact of Fang and Talon looks like, assuming it's still a part of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If I were the author of that section (and I'm not), I would probably make it about three separate Contracts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-30T19:37:53-07:00","id":245143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts?p=245127#post245127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> If I were the author of that section (and I'm not), I would probably make it about three separate Contracts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very interesting... Given the way that you see Contracts being shaken up into individual powers rather than suites, what mechanical (rather than narrative) nice would you consider Goblin Contracts filling? Greater power-to-price ration at the cost of unreliability?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-30T20:08:25-07:00","id":245150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>That Other Guy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts?p=245143#post245143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Very interesting... Given the way that you see Contracts being shaken up into individual powers rather than suites, what mechanical (rather than narrative) nice would you consider Goblin Contracts filling? Greater power-to-price ration at the cost of unreliability?</div> </div> </div> </div>not trying to be rude, but i think &quot;niche&quot; is the word you're looking for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/885-bwgustaf","name":"bwgustaf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-30T20:37:17-07:00","id":245158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts?p=245127#post245127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I were the author of that section (and I'm not), I would probably make it about three separate Contracts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm... Jumping off from that, I thought I'd run through a couple of mechanics-free mockups of the 1e 5-dot clause for Fang &amp; Talon. Mostly to see if I have some sort of grasp on things. Having typed them out, I definitely prefer the b-take, where the Favored Seeming is likely ideal, but the others are great within their niches. In the a-take, there is basically no reason you would ever want to take anything else, which isn't very interesting. Also, yes, I was very lazy in putting those together. &gt;.&gt; Just plopped 'em into the spoiler.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Contract of Beast (4-5 dots)</b></span><br /> Turn into an animal! Pick a species/type of beast on purchase, with multiple purchases allowed.<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">a) The Favored Seeming is objectively the best of the lot.<br /> Ogre: You become a beast known for its strength or ferocity.<br /> Elemental: Nope! Pay an Experience point for another Seeming's manifestation.<br /> Fairest: You become a beast known for its beauty or grace.<br /> Darkling: You become a beast known for dwelling in dark places or sneakiness.<br /> Beast: Pick whichever animal you like. Favored Seeming.<br /> Wizened: You become a beast known for small size or hard labor.<br /> </div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">b) The Favored Seeming is the most generally useful, but isn't better in all cases.<br /> Ogre: You become a particularly strong and fierce specimen.<br /> Elemental: Nope! Pay an Experience point for another Seeming's manifestation.<br /> Fairest: You become a particularly beautiful or graceful specimen.<br /> Darkling: You become a particularly stealthy or frightening specimen.<br /> Beast: You become a paragon of a specimen.* Favored Seeming.<br /> Wizened: You become a particularly small specimen or one particularly well suited to labor.</div> <br /> * I imagine something like &quot;this Seeming gets +1's to all actions/soak/whatever performed as an animal, the other 4 get +2's to actions/characteristics within their niches.&quot; And/Or Beasts can pick multiple species/types per purchase?</div></div> </div> </div><br /> It also made me think of another question, though I freely admit it's probably getting preeeetty nitty-gritty into mechanics to be able to comment. Not even sure what it would mean, honestly. Someone can more buy multiple Seemings for a given Contract at an extra Experience each. Is it possible for a Changeling who knows multiple Seemings for a given Contract to benefit from all of them with one activation, if applicable? Possibly with some extra cost (if Catches give options, perhaps activating an additional known Seeming might be a way)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":".  Reorganization, etc. 08-30-2014, 11:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-31T03:51:00-07:00","id":245269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>bwgustaf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts?p=245150#post245150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">not trying to be rude, but i think &quot;niche&quot; is the word you're looking for.</div> </div> </div> </div>...it was a typo at 3:30am, it's very obvious you knew what I was saying so why bring up a single dropped letter?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-31T05:22:41-07:00","id":245285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>That Other Guy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts?p=245143#post245143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Very interesting... Given the way that you see Contracts being shaken up into individual powers rather than suites, what mechanical (rather than narrative) nice would you consider Goblin Contracts filling? Greater power-to-price ration at the cost of unreliability?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> High cost, high reward. Also, in-character cost, so you can immediately fill a dire need.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-31T18:29:50-07:00","id":245760,"title":"","content":"That's exactly what I pictured the Goblin Contracts as when my girlfriend first talked about Changeling during our holiday walks. Saw lots of potential there, but then the actual mechanics in 1e disappointed me a bit. It'll be nice to see it realized.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-31T21:48:29-07:00","id":245852,"title":"","content":"Regarding the &quot;one Seeming is less likely to manifest a given Contract&quot; aspect, I don't know that I'd agree. Seemings are a very broad umbrella, by design.<br /> <br /> Contracts of Strength don't seem right for the Wizened? What about the Dwarfs who use it when forging their terrible weapons? <br /> <br /> Contracts of Cunning seem wrong for Beasts? I've got a feline fellow in fetching footwear whose plans have plans in their plans, and a fox named Reynard over here who wants a word. <br /> <br /> Part of what I like about the Seemings (in 1st ed) is that they are large and contain multitudes. You need *some* guidance, but I'd hate to lose the flexibility in design from the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-31T23:42:58-07:00","id":245918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HobbitGuy1420</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts?p=245852#post245852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding the &quot;one Seeming is less likely to manifest a given Contract&quot; aspect, I don't know that I'd agree. Seemings are a very broad umbrella, by design.<br /> <br /> Contracts of Strength don't seem right for the Wizened? What about the Dwarfs who use it when forging their terrible weapons?<br /> <br /> Contracts of Cunning seem wrong for Beasts? I've got a feline fellow in fetching footwear whose plans have plans in their plans, and a fox named Reynard over here who wants a word.<br /> <br /> Part of what I like about the Seemings (in 1st ed) is that they are large and contain multitudes. You need *some* guidance, but I'd hate to lose the flexibility in design from the game.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I see it as inherently more, not less. Contracts receive five variations here, instead of one. <br /> <br /> I think assuming a dwarf weaponsmith has to be Wizened is limiting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-01T00:46:06-07:00","id":245937,"title":"","content":"My concern is that the strength of the favored Seeming shouldn\u2019t come from the Contract, but from th Seeming. What I mean by that is that an Ogre with the Contract of Strength shouldn\u2019t be more effective because he has the Ogre\u2019s version of the Contract of Strength, but because he\u2019s an Ogre. That is, the Ogre\u2019s version of the Contract of Strength shouldn\u2019t be any more attractive to a Fairest or a Darkling than the Fairest or Darkling version is; but it <i>should</i> be more attractice to an Ogre than the other versions are. That was the reason behind my earlier suggestion: if the Ogre gets more out of Ogre Strength than the other Seemings do, then you\u2019ve got a case where Ogres are encouraged to take Strength; if <i>everyone</i> gets more out of Ogre Strength than they do out of the other Seemings\u2019 versions of Strength, you get a temptation to always spend an Experience to gain access to the favored Seeming\u2019s aspect of a Seeming Contract. <br /> <br /> Am I making sense, or am I straying too close to the dreaded White Room?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-01T02:31:16-07:00","id":246017,"title":"","content":"Dwarven blacksmiths are totally Wizened. They are the platonic Wizened.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts?p=245937#post245937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My concern is that the strength of the favored Seeming shouldn\u2019t come from the Contract, but from th Seeming. What I mean by that is that an Ogre with the Contract of Strength shouldn\u2019t be more effective because he has the Ogre\u2019s version of the Contract of Strength, but because he\u2019s an Ogre. That is, the Ogre\u2019s version of the Contract of Strength shouldn\u2019t be any more attractive to a Fairest or a Darkling than the Fairest or Darkling version is; but it <i>should</i> be more attractice to an Ogre than the other versions are. That was the reason behind my earlier suggestion: if the Ogre gets more out of Ogre Strength than the other Seemings do, then you\u2019ve got a case where Ogres are encouraged to take Strength; <b>if <i>everyone</i> gets more out of Ogre Strength than they do out of the other Seemings\u2019 versions of Strength, you get a temptation to always spend an Experience to gain access to the favored Seeming\u2019s aspect of a Seeming Contract.</b><br /> <br /> Am I making sense, or am I straying too close to the dreaded White Room?</div> </div> </div> </div>This strikes me as a really good point.<br /> <br /> If Ores get a bonus to Strength rolls, for example, they might inherently do better on Strength-based Contract rolls.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","name":"MugaSofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar877_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-01T03:34:37-07:00","id":246056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MugaSofer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts?p=246017#post246017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dwarven blacksmiths are totally Wizened. They are the platonic Wizened.<br /> <br /> <br /> This strikes me as a really good point.<br /> <br /> If Ores get a bonus to Strength rolls, for example, they might inherently do better on Strength-based Contract rolls.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That would functionally have the same end result. If they have a higher Strength, they'll buy Contracts that take advantage of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-01T04:46:47-07:00","id":246079,"title":"","content":"Just for the sake of clarity: I wasn\u2019t referring to the Strength attribute anywhere in my last post. Let\u2019s use a different example: a hypothetical Contract of Violence. Nearly every Seeming has its own invocation of this Contract, except perhaps the Fairest (who are more inclined to destroy reputations than to hurt people); for instance, the Bestial invocation of Violence includes claws and fangs; the Elemental invocation imbues the attack with elemental power (flaming swords, fists of stone, etc.) But Violence is what Ogres are all about; and when an Ogre invokes the Contract of Violence, mayhem ensues. <br /> <br /> The challenge is why, say, a Fairest who invests in the Contract of Violence wouldn\u2019t always go with the Ogre\u2019s version. Three possibilities: one is that the Ogre\u2019s version of Violence is specifically written to leverage whatever Blessing the Ogre receives; another is that the Ogre\u2019s version comes in two stages: the version that you get if you\u2019re an Ogre (which is designed to be superior to the other four), and a version that other Seemings get if they spend an Experience to access the Ogre version (which is a watered-down version of what Ogres get, designed to be on par with the other four); finally, it may be that the Ogre\u2019s version of Violence is exclusive to the Ogre, and that <i>nobody</i> gets to spend an Experience to get access to it: in order to revel in Violence the way an Ogre does, you need to <i>be an Ogre</i>. <br /> <br /> I personally don\u2019t like the first option, because I see a properly written Seeming Contract incorporating whatever a given Seeming\u2019s strengths happen to be: Ogre Violence takes into account an Ogre\u2019s raw destructive potential; but Bestial Violence should be, well, bestial violence. And so on. <br /> <br /> The second option is what I originally proposed. Its downside is the added complexity: Every Seeming Contract writeup would need, say, an extra paragraph for its favored Seeming, describing what additional benefits you get if you actually <i>are</i> that Seeming; or conversely, you might need a paragraph to describe which of the benefits are toned down or removed if you\u2019re <i>not</i> that Seeming. <br /> <br /> The third option has the drawback(?) that Ogre Violence is exclusive to Ogres; however, this means that it can be made as potent as you like without worrying about it becoming unduly attractive to other Seemings. This would be the simplest option, I think: all you\u2019d need would be to modify the \u201cspend an Experience to gain another aspect of the Contract\u201d rule to forbid purchasing the Favored Seeming\u2019s invocation. In short, replace \u201cfavored\u201d with \u201cexclusive\u201d.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>EDIT:</b> with the removal of the five-step \u201cladder of clauses\u201d for Universal Contacts, perhaps the term \u201cclause\u201d could be repurposed, for use by Seeming and possibly Court Contracts: the aforementioned Violence Contract would have an Ogre clause, a Darkling clause, a Wizened clause, a Bestial clause, and an Elemental clause; a hypothetical \u201cEternal Season\u201d Contract might have a Summer clause, a Winter clause, a Spring clause, and an Autumn clause (though in the case of Court Contracts, all clauses would be exclusive to the appropriate Mantle or Goodwill: no Court would be excluded, but no Court would be preferred either; you\u2019d have multiple distinct \u201cflavors\u201d of a common theme).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 09-01-2014, 07:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-01T05:55:42-07:00","id":246098,"title":"","content":"I'm probably going to get flak for this, but I do not like this fundamental change to how Contracts function.<br /> <br /> A Contract should feel like a Contract. Contracts don't change their wording based on who signs them. In 1e, a Contract is literally that. It's a contract with the fundamental forces of the world, signed by one's inherent nature as a Changeling and the Arcadia they escaped from.<br /> <br /> Having five different versions of each contract detracts from that theme. I would rather the idea that these are contracts be reinforced, rather than relegating them to just another power set.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-01T06:21:10-07:00","id":246110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts?p=246098#post246098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm probably going to get flak for this, but I do not like this fundamental change to how Contracts function.<br /> <br /> A Contract should feel like a Contract. Contracts don't change their wording based on who signs them. In 1e, a Contract is literally that. It's a contract with the fundamental forces of the world, signed by one's inherent nature as a Changeling and the Arcadia they escaped from.<br /> <br /> Having five different versions of each contract detracts from that theme. I would rather the idea that these are contracts be reinforced, rather than relegating them to just another power set.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have to say, I'm having much the same feeling. I can see the arguments as to how these are still Contracts (&quot;The signatories of the first party gain such-and-such benefit in addition to the aforementioned clauses&quot;), but they feel more like a bloodline power than a legal document. It was one thing that actually really worked about Changeling's 1-5 Clauses power set. It felt a lot more natural to slowly be gaining access to the disparate Clauses in that manner.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-01T08:46:17-07:00","id":246170,"title":"","content":"I actually have to agree, I'm not sure I'm super-comfortable with the entirety of Changeling contracts being unordered and assorted in this way. Feels a bit like it's invoking an edge of Demon or Vampire Bloodlines here (which, while awesome are entirely different games). Barring the problems with disparities in contract power levels, I would say it is convincingly the most mechanically solid set of powers (barring a few whiffs) in NWOD1.0, and the tiered progression coupled with the catch system helped it immensely. I can't say I've ever genuinely been stumped for how I'd want to build a changeling with a set of contracts that do something I want outside of Archmage-level worldbending.<br /> <br /> It was also a comprehensively simple system to explain to players new to the game, with each series having a general theme and each clause of the series being able to be easily digested as a one-sentence function of how they work (trust me! I've been working on cheat-sheets of contracts for a Changeling LARP.) There's a bit of duplication that could probably be cut down, especially with the Seasonal contracts in mind, but overall it works really well.<br /> <br /> While I could be convinced otherwise, I don't think it is one factor necessarily worth changing just for the sake of change.<br /> <br /> At this point, I think if you want more grab-baggy type powers, a revamp of Goblin Contracts would be worthwhile. And revamped in a way that they're no longer the fastest way to throw out 50XP outside of Character Death.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1462,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","user":"Xenesis","date":". 09-01-2014, 11:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-01T09:01:13-07:00","id":246177,"title":"","content":"IDK, I'm having trouble thinking of Contacts that would work better split up that way, but if there are some good examples ... MachineIV, do you have even some vague outlines of Seeming Contracts you could show us that really wouldn't work as Universal Contracts?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts?p=246056#post246056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That would functionally have the same end result. If they have a higher Strength, they'll buy Contracts that take advantage of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, that's the idea, IIUC.<br /> <br /> It's not the <i>same</i> result, though, because as Data pointed out above the &quot;favoured Kith&quot; idea has some unintended results.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> OK, let's use the sample Contract, just to make it clear we're spitballing:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts#post242936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Contract of Strength (2 dots)</b></span><br /> Makes you strong!<br /> Ogre: You get a direct Strength boost. Bam. Favored Seeming for this one.<br /> Elemental: You can draw on an example of your element to use its Structure instead of your dice pool for feats of strength.<br /> Fairest: When someone makes you look bad, your next strength action gets their successes added to yours.<br /> Darkling: When taking an action when nobody sees you, add your Stealth to your Strength.<br /> Beast: Grow a Size. Gain a Strength. Gain a Stamina.<br /> Wizened: Too bad, so sad. If you want Contract of Strength, pay an extra Experience and take another Seeming's manifestation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now, imagine I'm a Fairest Draconic. A beautiful sparkly dragon. Clearly, I need to go out-of-Kith for this one, since the Fairest version doesn't fit my concept.<br /> <br /> Now, being a Dragonic, clearly the best fit for my character is the Beast version. Dragons are big and strong. <i>But </i>the Ogre version is explicitly better than the others - if I don't buy it, I'll be significantly less <i>strong</i>. I have to choose between effectiveness and what fits my character.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> OK, scrap that, and imagine for a second that it works like this instead:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Contract of Strength (2 dots)</b></span><br /> <br /> Strength + Wyrd<br /> <br /> Makes you strong!<br /> Ogre: You get a small Strength boost.<br /> Elemental: You can draw on an example of your element to use its Structure instead of your dice pool for feats of strength.<br /> Fairest: When someone makes you look bad, your next strength action gets their successes added to yours.<br /> Darkling: When taking an action when nobody sees you, add your Stealth to your Strength.<br /> Beast: Grow a Size. Gain a Strength. Gain a Stamina.<br /> Wizened: You get a Strength boost when using Crafts or Weaponry. </div> </div> </div>Now, as a big strong dragon, clearly I want to buy up Strength anyway. So this Contract will work well for me - which makes sense, since it's a good fit for my character! Now, I <i>could</i> buy the Ogre version, but since they're all equally powerful, I go with the one that fits my concept best - the Beast version.<br /> <br /> Now, it's still inherently easier for a Ogre to use this Contract than for most characters; but that's because they're the type of Changeling that <i>would</i>, not because they bought the most effective version. Any Changeling can be that sort of character, and be about as effective, although without the Ogre Boon it'll be harder; and they can use <i>the right version of the Contract for them to do it.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":877,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","user":"MugaSofer","date":". 09-10-2014, 07:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","name":"MugaSofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar877_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-01T09:42:08-07:00","id":246193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts?p=246098#post246098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm probably going to get flak for this, but I do not like this fundamental change to how Contracts function.<br /> <br /> A Contract should feel like a Contract. Contracts don't change their wording based on who signs them. In 1e, a Contract is literally that. It's a contract with the fundamental forces of the world, signed by one's inherent nature as a Changeling and the Arcadia they escaped from.<br /> <br /> Having five different versions of each contract detracts from that theme. I would rather the idea that these are contracts be reinforced, rather than relegating them to just another power set.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here's the thing: they kind of already had a difference between who signed.<br /> <br /> Now, granted, the difference is EXP; a changeling who has sympathy with the contract gets to buy it for cheaper. That said, it does create a precedence for differences in the contract based on who is using it.<br /> <br /> If I was going to nitpick this, it would be &quot;Why do these differences in who signs them correlate to the Seemings?&quot;, but I like the change, so I'm not going to overtly sweat over it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-01T09:46:11-07:00","id":246195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MugaSofer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts?p=246017#post246017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dwarven blacksmiths are totally Wizened. They are the platonic Wizened.<br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno, I could make a compelling argument for Ogres and Darklings too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-01T10:23:30-07:00","id":246209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts?p=246195#post246195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I dunno, I could make a compelling argument for Ogres and Darklings too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also Elementals. Gnomes being tinkery has such strong press that it tends to bury the &quot;Paracelsian earth-spirits&quot; aspect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-01T10:25:04-07:00","id":246210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts?p=246193#post246193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's the thing: they kind of already had a difference between who signed.<br /> <br /> Now, granted, the difference is EXP; a changeling who has sympathy with the contract gets to buy it for cheaper. That said, it does create a precedence for differences in the contract based on who is using it.<br /> <br /> If I was going to nitpick this, it would be &quot;Why do these differences in who signs them correlate to the Seemings?&quot;, but I like the change, so I'm not going to overtly sweat over it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The contract still functions exactly the same. It's just harder to buy into it, since one doesn't already have a working &quot;business relationship&quot; with that particular facet of reality if it's non-affinity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-01T10:27:32-07:00","id":246211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MugaSofer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts?p=246017#post246017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dwarven blacksmiths are totally Wizened. They are the platonic Wizened.</div> </div> </div> </div> Then play them as a Wizened - but there's nothing preventing someone else from taking the Dwarven Smith kith and coming up with a Fairest or something.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-01T10:44:10-07:00","id":246229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts?p=246210#post246210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The contract still functions exactly the same. It's just harder to buy into it, since one doesn't already have a working &quot;business relationship&quot; with that particular facet of reality if it's non-affinity.</div> </div> </div> </div>I said there's a precedence, not an exact 1:1.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-01T11:03:15-07:00","id":246238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts?p=246079#post246079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just for the sake of clarity: I wasn\u2019t referring to the Strength attribute anywhere in my last post. Let\u2019s use a different example: a hypothetical Contract of Violence. Nearly every Seeming has its own invocation of this Contract, except perhaps the Fairest (who are more inclined to destroy reputations than to hurt people); for instance, the Bestial invocation of Violence includes claws and fangs; the Elemental invocation imbues the attack with elemental power (flaming swords, fists of stone, etc.) But Violence is what Ogres are all about; and when an Ogre invokes the Contract of Violence, mayhem ensues.<br /> <br /> The challenge is why, say, a Fairest who invests in the Contract of Violence wouldn\u2019t always go with the Ogre\u2019s version. Three possibilities: one is that the Ogre\u2019s version of Violence is specifically written to leverage whatever Blessing the Ogre receives; another is that the Ogre\u2019s version comes in two stages: the version that you get if you\u2019re an Ogre (which is designed to be superior to the other four), and a version that other Seemings get if they spend an Experience to access the Ogre version (which is a watered-down version of what Ogres get, designed to be on par with the other four); finally, it may be that the Ogre\u2019s version of Violence is exclusive to the Ogre, and that <i>nobody</i> gets to spend an Experience to get access to it: in order to revel in Violence the way an Ogre does, you need to <i>be an Ogre</i>.<br /> <br /> [...]<br /> <br /> The second option is what I originally proposed. Its downside is the added complexity: Every Seeming Contract writeup would need, say, an extra paragraph for its favored Seeming, describing what additional benefits you get if you actually <i>are</i> that Seeming; or conversely, you might need a paragraph to describe which of the benefits are toned down or removed if you\u2019re <i>not</i> that Seeming.<br /> <br /> [...]</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This would be also my favored option - some little add on for Ogre only while activating the favored contract.<br /> However i am worried about the wordcount - you are &quot;still&quot; actually writing 6 versions of the contract (all 4 other kiths, Ogre for Ogres, Ogre for non-Ogres.)<br /> <br /> Some simple alternatives which do not add too much to the wordcount: <br /> <br /> Ogres which use the contract of Violence (the Ogre facet, or also all the facets)...<br /> <br /> 1) Are already satisfying the catch, so they need not to spend glamour or willpower. <br /> <br /> DOWNSIDE: you don't have to use catches, and using catches is fun.<br /> Moreover, a character has an incentive in buying &quot;seeming&quot; contract which are really expensive, since the advantage is enhanced.<br /> <br /> 2) May roll the contract activation with the Rote quality, or with 8-again.<br /> <br /> DOWNSIDE: it may be actually too powerful - 8 again or rote with a good amount of dices is quite difficult to be resisted.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1304-baroqo","name":"Baroqo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-01T11:15:05-07:00","id":246246,"title":"","content":"Earlier, someone suggested multiple possible benefits for using a Catch, with \u201cyou don\u2019t have to spend any Glamour\u201d being the pedestrian choice. If Dave decides to go with something like this, you could have the Ogre get one of the Catch\u2019s possible benefits automatically, <i>plus</i> another benefit if he uses the Catch. DOWNSIDE: this relies on the Catch always offering a choice of benefits.<br /> <br /> Granting a special quality (9 again, 8 again, rote) to a favored Contract is a fairly simple and consistent option \u2014 but it potentially lacks flavor in the same way that a \u201cmore dice\u201d solution lacks flavor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 09-01-2014, 03:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-01T11:32:54-07:00","id":246257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts?p=246211#post246211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Then play them as a Wizened - but there's nothing preventing someone else from taking the Dwarven Smith kith and coming up with a Fairest or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, of course. For example, Thorin Oakenshield (in the new Hobbit movies, at least) is probably a Fairest.<br /> <br /> I just really really don't want that to be locked out by the game mechanics, because it's the thing that sells me on Wizened in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":877,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","user":"MugaSofer","date":". 09-01-2014, 02:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","name":"MugaSofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar877_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-01T12:02:07-07:00","id":246288,"title":"","content":"You\u2019re not locked out; you\u2019re just required to spend an extra Experience.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-01T15:46:24-07:00","id":246409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts?p=246170#post246170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I could be convinced otherwise, I don't think it is one factor necessarily worth changing just for the sake of change.</div> </div> </div> </div>Please, read generously. Never assume something's being done for the sake of doing it. <br /> <br /> It's not being done for the sake of change. It's being done because the five dot tiered structure led to forced levels, overlap, negation, speed bumps, powers that don't really fit thematically with what they're supposed to be, and boring abilities in the way of interesting abilities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-01T17:03:07-07:00","id":246459,"title":"","content":"I'm maximum excited about this idea. I always thought one of the cooler things about Changelings was the more flexible/less direct nature of their powers as opposed to...well, non-mages, really. Like, here's this random Wizened Soldier who took a few dots in Contracts of Seperation, so handcuffs slide right off. <br /> <br /> Individual contracts, I feel, lends itself to that idea. Changeling has always been super varied in character concept, and being able to pick and choose individual abilities without being shoehorned in to random, seemingly unrelated prerequisites is nothing but good. Also nothing wrong with a more unique progression.<br /> <br /> It is WAY too early to be psyched about this game, and yet I am!!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-01T17:07:22-07:00","id":246463,"title":"","content":"Also, Davis, try not to get upset at any negativity from posters here (if you even are; I would be). Forums be crazy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-01T17:13:19-07:00","id":246466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enokh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts?p=246463#post246463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, Davis, try not to get upset at any negativity from posters here (if you even are; I would be). Forums be crazy.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> We're cool. I just need to keep things productive. Assuming arbitrary motivations is a quick way down a really bad path, though. Particularly since reasons have been addressed a few times already.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-01T18:10:09-07:00","id":246483,"title":"","content":"True that. Criticism is way better than blind negativity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-01T18:19:07-07:00","id":246496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enokh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts?p=246483#post246483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True that. Criticism is way better than blind negativity.</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't seen any blind negativity thus far. It's important not to dismiss dissenting opinions as &quot;blindly negative.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-01T18:21:48-07:00","id":246497,"title":"","content":"I was actually referring to the &quot;changing for the sake of changing&quot; comment by another poster. I'm sorry you thought I was referring to you. Love me some dissenting opinions; its hardly feedback if all anyone says is how awesome things are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-01T18:54:28-07:00","id":246549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts?p=246409#post246409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Please, read generously. Never assume something's being done for the sake of doing it.<br /> <br /> It's not being done for the sake of change. It's being done because the five dot tiered structure led to forced levels, overlap, negation, speed bumps, powers that don't really fit thematically with what they're supposed to be, and boring abilities in the way of interesting abilities.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that makes me feel a bit better about it. Maybe it was the 3am insomnia, or maybe I just don't quite grok the discussion style in this thread so much but it didn't come off that way to me - like I said in the prior post of mine, I still feel that the 1.0 Contract system is one of the least busted parts about Changeling and it did feel when I posted that, that this was decided upon because the other gamelines were doing it.<br /> <br /> I still have some general misgivings about it in that this new system as a whole seems significantly more complicated (kind of in that Geist Key-Manifestation sort of way). Having tons of subtle variations of powers is going to get confusing, I feel. I do like the strong thematic value of the contract-sets as it is and I suppose I worry that if they're individual clauses with individual flavours for each seeming that they're just not going to resonate with me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-01T19:31:22-07:00","id":246561,"title":"","content":"Personally, I prefer five subtle (or not so subtle) variations on a theme that I can take in any order I want<sup>*</sup> over a chain of powers that must be purchased in a specific sequence whether you want to or not. Parallel clauses rather than serial clauses. <br /> <br /> In fact, I wouldn\u2019t mind if the notion were to be expanded to the occasional Universal Contract as well, with \u201cvariations on a theme\u201d that don\u2019t fit the Seeming or Court model in terms of how they vary nevertheless being presented as parallel clauses where you pick one to start with and get additional ones for one Experience each. That said, that\u2019s strictly a hypothetical on my part, as I can\u2019t readily think of anything off the top of my head. <br /> <br /> The problem I have with <b>Geist</b>\u2019s Keys and Manifestations model is the rigidity involved: if I want Industrial Shroud and Stygian Graveyard, I automatically get Stygian Shroud and Industrial Graveyard as well, whether I want em or not. Contracts with parallel clauses don\u2019t hace at problem. <br /> <hr />* Assuming I take more than one at all; I see little point in one character taking multiple powers that essentially do the same thing, which is why one more Experience per variation after the first makes sense to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 09-01-2014, 10:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-01T21:52:53-07:00","id":246641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts?p=246561#post246561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The problem I have with <b>Geist</b>\u2019s Keys and Manifestations model is the rigidity involved: if I want Industrial Shroud and Stygian Graveyard, I automatically get Stygian Shroud and Industrial Graveyard as well, whether I want em or not. Contracts with parallel clauses don\u2019t hace at problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, wait, wait.<br /> <br /> You can go for the things you want, and as a result you get free extra powers?<br /> <br /> <i>How is that a problem? </i>It's not like you're even paying anything more for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-01T22:04:58-07:00","id":246646,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s the opposite problem from the \u201cchain of powers\u201d approach, where you\u2019re forced to pay for powers that you don\u2019t want. The common thread is that you potentially end up with powers that don\u2019t fit your character concept, because the mechanics insist that you take them; the fact that you have to pay for them in the \u201cchains of powers\u201d approach just adds insult to injury.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-01T22:11:20-07:00","id":246651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts?p=246646#post246646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It\u2019s the opposite problem from the \u201cchain of powers\u201d approach, where you\u2019re forced to pay for powers that you don\u2019t want. The common thread is that you potentially end up with powers that don\u2019t fit your character concept, because the mechanics insist that you take them; the fact that you have to pay for them in the \u201cchains of powers\u201d approach just adds insult to injury.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that Geist doesn't quite illustrate what you are saying beyond the fact that buying a Manifestation, which gave you 2+ powers, was part of the logic for more expensive Manifestations.<br /> <br /> I mean, it works in the sense that a linear progression was used for that, so if you wanted Industrial Marionette 4 you had to buy Marionette 1-3, that's a related problem. But the fact that, since you have the Pyre Flame key you also get Pyre Flame Marionette 1-4 in your quest to get Industrial Marionette 4, doesn't parse.<br /> <br /> It's like saying &quot;Oh, you worked up to get a car you wanted? Here,have another car included with that&quot;. Even if the second car isn't what you wanted, you have to admit that having a second car on hand as a result of you buying the first is pretty nifty.<br /> <br /> Unless it really is about how damn expensive Manifestations were, because then yeah, I see the problem.<br /> <br /> All of this is deviating from the topic, which I still really need to sit down and collect my thoughts on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-01T23:06:14-07:00","id":246662,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m a strong advocate for concept-centric character design, to the point that I\u2019ve developed an aversion against thinking primarily in terms of \u201ccost effectiveness\u201d. That is, I\u2019m willing and able to do so when the game system forces me to; but my preference is to put \u201cdoes it fit my concept?\u201d as the top priority, and \u201cdoes it fit my budget?\u201d as a distant second. In particular, I dislike the mindset of \u201cthe point budget constrains what I can get; so I\u2019m going to take everything that it lets me take, and I\u2019ll feel grateful for it.\u201d It\u2019s a symptom of an adversarial relationship between the player and the character creation system. <br /> <br /> Admittedly, it\u2019s nowhere near as serious a problem in Onyx Path\u2019s games as it is in, say, Hero System or GURPS, where I first developed the aversion. Still\u2026<br /> <br /> For <b>Geist</b>, I\u2019d want to revise the pricing structure downward while keeping the powers matrix, on the premise that a given Key will only automatically unlock one Manifestation: say, pay for each Manifestation once and for each Key once, choosing which Manifestation the Key unlocks when you acquire the Key; then pay a nominal fee (say, one Experience) for each additional Manifestation you have that a given Key unlocks \u2014 not unlike the \u201cpay an Experience for each additional clause of a Contract\u201d setup that David has proposed for <b>Changeling</b>. Which is the only relevance this tangent as to the thread\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-01T23:21:49-07:00","id":246669,"title":"","content":"Bringing it back around a bit\u2026<br /> <br /> I <i>liked</i> that striking outright new Contracts was a difficult thing that called for venturing deep into the Hedge and making a weighty sacrifice - it seemed a neat reflection of the admittedly loosely-defined aspects of developing new rites or ceremonies in Werewolf and Geist, and it forever marked your mien into the bargain. I'd be kind of sad to see the difficulty investment and attendant prestige such developments warranted go away completely. (I'm almost certain they won't, but it's a concern I thought was worth airing.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-01T23:48:27-07:00","id":246675,"title":"","content":"Agreed: creating new Contracts should be an accomplishment \u2014 unless it\u2019s a Goblin Contract, the lot of which I feel should be borderline-pledges in terms of ease of creation. That is, I wouldn\u2019t mind in the least if Goblin Contracts occupied a sort of middle ground between Pledges and Contracts. I\u2019d borrow heavily from the premise behind Goblin Pledges from <b>Rites of Spring</b>, though not necessarily in terms of specific mechanics: for instance, I\u2019d tend to favor prices that take the form of \u201cGoblin Contract\u201d-like activation costs, bundled with supernatural effects akin to what you can get from a Goblin Vow in 1e, but without any of the messiness of \u201cwhat happens if I break my side of the bargain?\u201d because your side (the activation cost) always gets satisfied first. <br /> <br /> But a Universal Contract, Seeming Contract, or Court Contract? Developing one should be the basis for a story or even a chronicle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-02T00:09:54-07:00","id":246684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts?p=246675#post246675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Agreed: creating new Contracts should be an accomplishment \u2014 unless it\u2019s a Goblin Contract, the lot of which I feel should be borderline-pledges in terms of ease of creation. That is, I wouldn\u2019t mind in the least if Goblin Contracts occupied a sort of middle ground between Pledges and Contracts. I\u2019d borrow heavily from the premise behind Goblin Pledges from <b>Rites of Spring</b>, though not necessarily in terms of specific mechanics: for instance, I\u2019d tend to favor prices that take the form of \u201cGoblin Contract\u201d-like activation costs, bundled with supernatural effects akin to what you can get from a Goblin Vow in 1e, but without any of the messiness of \u201cwhat happens if I break my side of the bargain?\u201d because your side (the activation cost) always gets satisfied first.<br /> <br /> But a Universal Contract, Seeming Contract, or Court Contract? Developing one should be the basis for a story or even a chronicle.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem with something like that being a basis for a chronicle is that you have a bunch of other bored people playing, because even if they're helping or involved, ultimately it comes down to it suiting one character best and them ultimately being the one 'penning' it.<br /> <br /> That said, I think it needs to be easier than in 1e, but not trivially so. THough I do agree goblin contracts being more towards the free form end of things would be nice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-02T09:28:12-07:00","id":246853,"title":"","content":"Do we need Seeming Contracts? I'd almost rather see just Universal and Court contracts and let Seeming suffice with other benefits. Anyone else agree?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-02T09:42:13-07:00","id":246857,"title":"","content":"I feel like you are alone in that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-02T10:24:55-07:00","id":246909,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure I'm wed to the idea that we need Seeming Contracts. Especially with the new take on Seemings that the 2e book is heading on.<br /> <br /> However, I'm not sure that getting rid of them is the right idea. I like the idea that some Contracts respond differently to different Seemings. It is a neat and interesting design space that can add flavor to the game.<br /> <br /> But maybe that's something to stress in how their defined/explained. Seeming Contracts are not &quot;Orge Contracts,&quot; and &quot;Beast Contracts,&quot; and &quot;Wizened Contracts.&quot; They're Contracts that have different base outputs for different Seemings; but those outputs are uneven.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-02T13:25:39-07:00","id":247099,"title":"","content":"Actually, I'm pretty sure you're wrong on that, Arcane. Quite a few people have expressed doubts about the whole &quot;Seeming Contract&quot; concept.<br /> <br /> Personally, I feel like I agree with Eberg, but I suspect the devs may have some really great ideas for Seeming Contracts I just haven't thought of. If a Contract or set of contracts really works better like that, I can't think of any reason to exclude the possibility. <i>Most </i>Contracts probably work best as Universal, so I assume that's how they'll stay.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":877,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","user":"MugaSofer","date":". 09-02-2014, 04:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","name":"MugaSofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar877_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-02T14:02:49-07:00","id":247110,"title":"","content":"That's why I said I Feel rather than I Think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-02T17:22:59-07:00","id":247273,"title":"","content":"I'm personally waiting for something in the Seeming Contract concept here to make me go 'THAT'S AWESOME' rather than 'eh, it's okay but it seems really complicated-slash-fiddly.'<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts?p=246684#post246684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The problem with something like that being a basis for a chronicle is that you have a bunch of other bored people playing, because even if they're helping or involved, ultimately it comes down to it suiting one character best and them ultimately being the one 'penning' it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, forging contracts would only make sense in a single-player adventure really. Or at least as is. Unless it can be reshaped to be some form of collective effort (Enterprise bargaining with facets of reality? :P ) I don't think it'd ever be something worth including in a game with more than one ST and one player.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-02T20:06:37-07:00","id":247391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>eberg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts?p=246853#post246853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do we need Seeming Contracts? I'd almost rather see just Universal and Court contracts and let Seeming suffice with other benefits. Anyone else agree?</div> </div> </div> </div>I really think bird changelings should be more capable of bird magic than not-bird changelings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-02T21:58:24-07:00","id":247467,"title":"","content":"That's more of an argument for Kith Contracts, not Seeming Contracts. A Seeming Contract that favors Beasts favors birds just as well as it favors turtles. While whatever aspect of &quot;bird magic&quot; we're talking about probably isn't unique to Beasts.<br /> <br /> Shouldn't a songbird Fairest have bird magic as a hawk Beast?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-03T16:16:04-07:00","id":248219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts?p=246409#post246409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Please, read generously. Never assume something's being done for the sake of doing it.<br /> <br /> It's not being done for the sake of change. It's being done because the five dot tiered structure led to forced levels, overlap, negation, speed bumps, powers that don't really fit thematically with what they're supposed to be, and boring abilities in the way of interesting abilities.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've just started reading and am very glad for the ideas you've shared. But I have to say something here: Is the five dot structure primarily to blame for any of those things? <br /> <br /> A tiered structure lends itself to orderly advancement and gradual mastery of a concept and helps maintain some semblance of power balance, particularly for crossover efforts. These concerns might be more important to STs and developers but they do matter.<br /> <br /> &quot;Speed bumps&quot; only seem to be a real issue with Contracts that lost their way, like Darkness. Likewise, &quot;boring abilities in the way of interesting abilities&quot; sounds like a sign that the <i>abilities </i>need more attention. These reasons reflect concerns that should be addressed, but I am not convinced that undoing a rather solid system is the way to go about it. Contracts that retain their thematic focuses and are built with usability in mind should take care of it.<br /> <br /> Being able to take Goblin Contracts in any order, however, was always a key and flavorful difference between the powers changelings are able to forge and those that goblins create with their own goals and ways in mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kismet's <a href=\"http://www.wod.kismetrose.com/\" target=\"_blank\">WOD</a> - <a href=\"http://www.dnd.kismetrose.com/\" target=\"_blank\">D&amp;D</a> - <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/BoundinDreams\" target=\"_blank\">C:tL</a> - <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/TheNamelessEmpire\" target=\"_blank\">M:tC</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/227-kismetrose","name":"KismetRose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar227_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-03T16:23:40-07:00","id":248225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KismetRose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts?p=248219#post248219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've just started reading and am very glad for the ideas you've shared. But I have to say something here: Is the five dot structure primarily to blame for any of those things?<br /> <br /> A tiered structure lends itself to orderly advancement and gradual mastery of a concept and helps maintain some semblance of power balance, particularly for crossover efforts. These concerns might be more important to STs and developers but they do matter.<br /> <br /> &quot;Speed bumps&quot; only seem to be a real issue with Contracts that lost their way, like Darkness. Likewise, &quot;boring abilities in the way of interesting abilities&quot; sounds like a sign that the <i>abilities </i>need more attention. These reasons reflect concerns that should be addressed, but I am not convinced that undoing a rather solid system is the way to go about it. Contracts that retain their thematic focuses and are built with usability in mind should take care of it.<br /> <br /> Being able to take Goblin Contracts in any order, however, was always a key and flavorful difference between the powers changelings are able to forge and those that goblins create with their own goals and ways in mind.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> In our experience, yes, it's the five dot structure. If, as a developer, you come up with an interesting idea for a power that you feel really warrants inclusion, the onus is then on you to craft four other powers. For example, Vampire's gone through tons of editions. None of the core Disciplines have gone without any sort of change, because some of the powers rendered each other redundant, were boring, or felt thematically out of place. But there are certainly powers we know we want vampires to have. After over 20 years, we're still feeling them out and tinkering with them in order to make that five dot progression feel right. If we're still struggling with that after 20 years and dozens of writers, the structure is probably to blame, yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-03T17:58:55-07:00","id":248320,"title":"","content":"To play devil's advocate, I can see a middle ground between &quot;grab bag powers&quot; and &quot;fixed 5-dot structure.&quot; Each Contract could have a variable number of clauses, between 1 and 5 (or however many). If a developer comes up with a really interesting idea for a power, it works fine as a one-dot effect. If said developer finds the full desired effect might be a bit too potent to go in one clause or feels there is additional space to explore there, the Contract could contain additional clauses that either expand the initial power or provide effects that synergize well with it. This would seem an effective way to eliminate some of the issues with the 5-dot structure while preserving the sense of orderly advancement that some people like.<br /> <br /> Sidebar: The Exalted fan in me might be showing, but I might even go further, to something like short Charm trees (emphasis on short), with powers leading to other powers or budding off into alternate applications or expansions as suits the Contract's theme and any internal logic. I just really enjoy growing into parts of a powerset that feel like they build on themselves in meaningful, interesting ways.<br /> <br /> For the record, I'm mostly spitballing in that last paragraph. I'm pleased with the deviation from the strict 5-dot structure. The more I think about it, the more I see cool possibilities with the new setup David has described. Including getting at some of what I consider the perks of alternatives I mentioned in the last paragraph. It seems very natural that some Contracts would have synergies with others (Catches could play into this, too), making up formal/informal groupings people might want to explore. Likewise, Seeming Contracts give anyone who's really gung-ho about the Contract's area a chance to expand their capabilities by buying the other 4-5 &quot;clauses&quot; fairly cheaply. This hinges on all of the Seeming &quot;clauses&quot; not feeling redundant with each other, but that shouldn't be too demanding.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-03T22:12:15-07:00","id":248552,"title":"","content":"This is called Brainspew, so I'll take advantage of that. I'll try not to get anyone wet.<br /> <br /> I'll remain a stalwart defender of the 5-dot progressive structure. The removal of the progression, but still having the thematic progression, was something that made me close Werewolf: the Forsaken and smack the hardcover against my forehead. I was so happy to see things finally get organized, and then... &quot;Nevermind! Fooled you!&quot; *thwack*<br /> <br /> Crunch first. Having the structure and progression enforces balance within the Contract. It reinforces the Knowing/Compelling &lt; Ruling / Shielding &lt; Un/Weaving &lt; Un/Making &lt; Mastery/Becoming structure that Mage laid out quite well. Several existing early contracts did this wonderfully (with some noted hiccups like Dream 1 and Darkness). Yes, Vampire has gone through 20+ years of refining, and still sees tweaks and changes. oWoD wasn't made with power balance between games in its original structure either (Lupines vs Garou, very different creatures). nWoD is, and one of the things that has kept me in the Storyteller System has been the steps taken for a proper system balance across each title. Throwing out structure just seems like an open invite for early power creep and the &quot;yeah, whatever, let's let them do this&quot; like Gifts from Apocalypse that stray off to unthematic regions.<br /> Skipping levels in the progression also stunts the curve. Speaking as a player rather than a GM, knowing how to use the low level abilities effectively sets you up for applications of the higher end. Jumping right into the deep end of a contract will just leave you to drown in your own ideas, wondering &quot;why did I pick this again?&quot; Your mileage may vary, but I'm drawing on my experiences specifically with Reflections. It goes somewhere, and I'd be in unfamiliar waters if I jumped right into reaching through a reflective surface to grab the knife in my bathroom's toothbrush holder if I hadn't gone through the experience of grabbing my television and rewinding to find out how the hell I ended up on my couch when I was left for dead in the Hedge the night before.<br /> <br /> The Universal/Seeming contract XP structure fits with other game lines. You are X, and that means you're going to have an easier time being good at Y and Z, but not W. Oh, you're an A? B, C, and D are your strong points, but you're going to have to work harder for Y and Z. That's just core structure (Clan Disciplines, Path Arcana, for example).<br /> <br /> Coming up with a single ability that is thematic for Changelings to have is not a complete contract. If it's not part of a progressive theme, don't force it to be one. Have it be a single power similar to a Goblin Contract, but nix the drawbacks. Let's just call them Cantrips for the sake of argument (and pandering to CtD fans). X cantrip costs 2 dots, and lets you... know what a token/trifle/goblin fruit does. More successes means more info (drawbacks, catch, etc). Has a catch. Could you develop a whole &quot;Contracts of the Hedge&quot;? Sure. Do you need to? No. A Universal one-off 'Contract' that makes sense for Changelings to have and to learn, but isn't part of a larger structure and thematic whole. Single clause? Ok, cool. I can deal with that, but it's not a 'Contract'.<br /> <br /> This leads into the fluff.<br /> <br /> A Contract is a deal made with a concept. The seasons, Stone, elements, darkness, mirrors, and so forth. Somewhere, some changeling got the hutspah enough to address something and say &quot;Hey, let's make a deal&quot;, because they're insane enough to do that... and conceptual things (*cough*totems*cough*) like to make deals in return for reinforcement of what they are, and what they represent. A Contract is a complete promise to uphold and utilize the very concept it's made with. Now, the original promise may have happened long, long ago in a kingdom far, far away, but it's still the same promise. &quot;I solemnly swear to make Dreams special&quot;. &quot;I will become the mirror and reflect both friend and foe&quot;. &quot;Stone is solid, unmoving, and unbreakable. This is what I shall become&quot;. A modern changeling might not even realize that the push of emotional energy (Glamour) into fueling the power of a concept is empowering the very thing the Contract was bargained with, but they're doing exactly that! Centuries down the line, pushing the fuel of passion to twist someone's desires another direction empowers the concepts of a Fleeting Spring, and young fickle lovers. Even if no one else is around to witness it, the concept, the very core, knows.<br /> &quot;Good job. Have a cookie. Oh, you've been doing a really good job? Let's see what you can do with a bit more oomph.&quot; And the contract progresses, following the line of the original promise. In time, you've grown in your upholding of the Contract until you're on par with the one who sealed the deal in the first place, and you have the full access to the concept's gifts. You're a champion of [insert stuff here]! Behold the awesome!<br /> Divorcing the progressive structure cheats the deal. You don't learn your way around using the concept creatively (which many clauses need to be utilized as more than parlor tricks). You just jump right in and say &quot;Ha! I'm a giant fireball! FEAR ME!&quot; without having any progression up to that point that proves to the concept that you'll even know WTF you're doing. See above about the curve. You start the promise, the Contract, and you fulfill your end of the bargain through application, and get paid with access to more and greater.<br /> <br /> Ok. That's my spew for now. I'll get the mop.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3805-nlight","name":"NLight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-03T22:40:00-07:00","id":248578,"title":"","content":"Err\u2026 the idea of the Brain Spew is \u201cthe author spews his thoughts, then the rest of us provide feedback on how to refine and/or expand on those thoughts\u201d. I\u2019m assuming that the author has already decided on the general approach by the time he posts one of these threads; so rejecting the general approach isn\u2019t constructive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-03T23:06:42-07:00","id":248622,"title":"","content":"So, I know it might sound a little obtuse, but I'm having trouble seeing the problems that those fervently defending the 5 dot progression seem to think is there. The only reason to claim a full Contract needs 5 dots is because it used to be that way, there's no 'a single dot isn't a contract'. You don't sign a contract with a loan provider and expect that they'll also provide you investment advice, nor do you sign a car ownership deal and expect a chauffeur to come with it, so I don't know why a single power can't be considered a 'contract' with that element of the universe. It's simply going to be a smaller element, or a specific part of it, each time, and I think to say otherwise is to simply be embedded in the old system rather than looking at it from the perspective of what really makes the most sense.<br /> <br /> As for the mention of needing low level abilities to know how to use high level ones... what? Since when? Having Cloak of Elements doesn't in any way make you more 'prepared' to know how to transform into that element later. It's an entirely different thing. So I'm not really buying that either. Sure, they CAN be designed that way, and occasionally powers are, but I don't really think it's needed, nor does it fit the thematics of contracts anyway. There's no reason more fluid contract purchases can't build upon each other in a way each player defines for themselves.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490