ry, but I'm drawing on my experiences specifically with Reflections. It goes somewhere, and I'd be in unfamiliar waters if I jumped right into reaching through a reflective surface to grab the knife in my bathroom's toothbrush holder if I hadn't gone through the experience of grabbing my television and rewinding to find out how the hell I ended up on my couch when I was left for dead in the Hedge the night before.<br /> <br /> The Universal/Seeming contract XP structure fits with other game lines. You are X, and that means you're going to have an easier time being good at Y and Z, but not W. Oh, you're an A? B, C, and D are your strong points, but you're going to have to work harder for Y and Z. That's just core structure (Clan Disciplines, Path Arcana, for example).<br /> <br /> Coming up with a single ability that is thematic for Changelings to have is not a complete contract. If it's not part of a progressive theme, don't force it to be one. Have it be a single power similar to a Goblin Contract, but nix the drawbacks. Let's just call them Cantrips for the sake of argument (and pandering to CtD fans). X cantrip costs 2 dots, and lets you... know what a token/trifle/goblin fruit does. More successes means more info (drawbacks, catch, etc). Has a catch. Could you develop a whole &quot;Contracts of the Hedge&quot;? Sure. Do you need to? No. A Universal one-off 'Contract' that makes sense for Changelings to have and to learn, but isn't part of a larger structure and thematic whole. Single clause? Ok, cool. I can deal with that, but it's not a 'Contract'.<br /> <br /> This leads into the fluff.<br /> <br /> A Contract is a deal made with a concept. The seasons, Stone, elements, darkness, mirrors, and so forth. Somewhere, some changeling got the hutspah enough to address something and say &quot;Hey, let's make a deal&quot;, because they're insane enough to do that... and conceptual things (*cough*totems*cough*) like to make deals in return for reinforcement of what they are, and what they represent. A Contract is a complete promise to uphold and utilize the very concept it's made with. Now, the original promise may have happened long, long ago in a kingdom far, far away, but it's still the same promise. &quot;I solemnly swear to make Dreams special&quot;. &quot;I will become the mirror and reflect both friend and foe&quot;. &quot;Stone is solid, unmoving, and unbreakable. This is what I shall become&quot;. A modern changeling might not even realize that the push of emotional energy (Glamour) into fueling the power of a concept is empowering the very thing the Contract was bargained with, but they're doing exactly that! Centuries down the line, pushing the fuel of passion to twist someone's desires another direction empowers the concepts of a Fleeting Spring, and young fickle lovers. Even if no one else is around to witness it, the concept, the very core, knows.<br /> &quot;Good job. Have a cookie. Oh, you've been doing a really good job? Let's see what you can do with a bit more oomph.&quot; And the contract progresses, following the line of the original promise. In time, you've grown in your upholding of the Contract until you're on par with the one who sealed the deal in the first place, and you have the full access to the concept's gifts. You're a champion of [insert stuff here]! Behold the awesome!<br /> Divorcing the progressive structure cheats the deal. You don't learn your way around using the concept creatively (which many clauses need to be utilized as more than parlor tricks). You just jump right in and say &quot;Ha! I'm a giant fireball! FEAR ME!&quot; without having any progression up to that point that proves to the concept that you'll even know WTF you're doing. See above about the curve. You start the promise, the Contract, and you fulfill your end of the bargain through application, and get paid with access to more and greater.<br /> <br /> Ok. That's my spew for now. I'll get the mop.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not going to line item. But I pretty much disagree with most of this. While I appreciate the critique, I don't feel that these arguments make for a strong case for rehashing the old structure, in accordance with my vision for the project.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T07:31:04-07:00","id":248828,"title":"","content":"The 5-Dot tiered structure is appropriate to represent a singular skill or concept you gradually get better at. Changelign powers are presented as being more grab-bag-y &quot;You can do X thing because you made an agreement with Y concept to do X.&quot; Its not about progressing gradually in a skillset (other than making contracts themselves). Its about finding another beneficial contract you can participate in.<br /> <br /> 5-Dot Tier works in Blood and Smoke because each Discipline is really just one thing, then that one thing gets advancements or minor variants as the vampire levels up. Some exceptions apply, of course. Obfuscate 4 is measurably *better* at hiding themselves through vampire magic than Obfuscate 2. The differences of types of power are just to make that distinction felt more.<br /> <br /> Once you have a Contract with Potatos to grow spuds. You can't be better at that same exact contract to grow exploding spuds. The contract is the contract is the contract, with few exceptions. If you want exploding spuds, that costs extra (as a different contract). You aren't becoming better with your agreement, you are amending or expanding that. 5-Dot Tier system simple doesn't handle that as well.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T07:51:54-07:00","id":248861,"title":"","content":"Also, as with Gifts and Transmutations, there's no addition of the dot-rating to 1e Contract dicepools - and if I'm not misremembering the discussion of Firestorm/PtC2e, both of the preceding two are also moving to a largely non-five-dot-based structure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T08:23:00-07:00","id":248882,"title":"","content":"Not to beat this horse too dead, but on the progression vs. grab bag thing, we also know enough about Forsaken 2e to look at that in all this.<br /> <br /> Forsaken is taking a mixed approach of some 5-dot progression powers, and some not. I think this backs up a lot of the thoughts about breaking off the &quot;everything in 5-dot progression.&quot;<br /> <br /> In Forsaken 2e your Auspice's Moon Gift is a 5-dot progression where you get better at doing the core things for your Auspice (similar to SoulGambit's point), and Shadow Gifts which are available to everyone and contain five Facets that key off of the five types of Renown (more similar to the stated idea for the new Seeming Contracts without being slanted for specific splats directly).<br /> <br /> While I don't think that the 5-dot progression concept is so flawed that is never worth using (and clearly the nWOD 2e teams don't since 4/6 2e games still use them in some fashion so far), dropping it when the flaws are getting in the way too much of the design goals of the rules is a good thing. The 5-dot progressions aren't necessary for a nWOD supernatural game to work, so using that model should be done to support the design goals of the developers and authors, not because it is the default way the WOD systems tend to handle supernatural powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","user":"Heavy Arms","date":". 09-04-2014, 02:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T12:44:29-07:00","id":249066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts?p=248669#post248669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not going to line item. But I pretty much disagree with most of this. While I appreciate the critique, I don't feel that these arguments make for a strong case for rehashing the old structure, in accordance with my vision for the project.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's cool. Just wanted to sound off my $0.02 and perspective. Thank you for reading.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3805-nlight","name":"NLight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T16:43:45-07:00","id":249284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts?p=248882#post248882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While I don't think that the 5-dot progression concept is so flawed that is never worth using (and clearly the nWOD 2e teams don't since 4/6 2e games still use them in some fashion so far), dropping it when the flaws are getting in the way too much of the design goals of the rules is a good thing. The 5-dot progressions aren't necessary for a nWOD supernatural game to work, so using that model should be done to support the design goals of the developers and authors, not because it is the default way the WOD systems tend to handle supernatural powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, this is a big part of it. Could we do it? Sure. But it'd be a lot more work for the same outcomes. It'd result in more wasted space, and fewer interesting, divergent ideas surfacing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T16:51:56-07:00","id":249288,"title":"","content":"The five dot progression only really makes sense when it is tracking a single ability in which the character is improving. It works well for Mage, as each dot of an Arcana is representative of greater mastery, not a new ability. The same thought was applied to the Disciplines in Requiem 2.0, hence why the later powers all call back to and improve the lower dots. But for something like Contracts, which are each a discreet new power tied to a central theme, the five dot progression makes little sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T18:33:13-07:00","id":249347,"title":"","content":"So, in comparing Shadow Gifts to Seeming Contracts, I was wondering about something:<br /> <br /> Is there a way to make Seeming Contracts less mechanically slanted to a specific Seeming option being the best, and thus just something everyone will want to buy anyway, and making it more of a synergy between Seeming bonuses/powers that other Seemings wouldn't be able to get?<br /> <br /> With Shadow Gifts, the Facets are usually fairly even (at least so far from previews) in power/utility. But your splats, through which Renown they give/encourage you to grow, heavily influence which Facets you'll get a lot of bang out of and which you don't.<br /> <br /> If Seeming Contracts have Clauses that key off specific powers (aka Seeming blessings, though potentially Kith ones when that might be appropriate) rather than Seemings directly, they don't need to have imbalanced Clauses beyond that synergy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T18:43:04-07:00","id":249354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts?p=249347#post249347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, in comparing Shadow Gifts to Seeming Contracts, I was wondering about something:<br /> <br /> Is there a way to make Seeming Contracts less mechanically slanted to a specific Seeming option being the best, and thus just something everyone will want to buy anyway, and making it more of a synergy between Seeming bonuses/powers that other Seemings wouldn't be able to get?<br /> <br /> With Shadow Gifts, the Facets are usually fairly even (at least so far from previews) in power/utility. But your splats, through which Renown they give/encourage you to grow, heavily influence which Facets you'll get a lot of bang out of and which you don't.<br /> <br /> If Seeming Contracts have Clauses that key off specific powers (aka Seeming blessings, though potentially Kith ones when that might be appropriate) rather than Seemings directly, they don't need to have imbalanced Clauses beyond that synergy.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's a viable approach. I don't see why we couldn't look at it like that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T18:52:46-07:00","id":249365,"title":"","content":"It doesn\u2019t have to be either/or. Some Seeming Contracts work equally well for any Seeming (albeit differently for each), and have neither favored nor missing clauses; others naturally gravitate toward one Seeming, and work as you\u2019ve described.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-05T06:27:47-07:00","id":249727,"title":"","content":"I fully support being able to pick and choose what levels of a contract you'd like. Flavourwise, I didn't quite understand why you needed to understand contracts progressively, instead of scouring through a contract for the part you wanted, learning that, and then disregarding the rest. Even most durance didn't need it. Every progressive 5 dot contract always had at least 1 contract you never really used, so it seemed unnecessary to grab it (but required).<br /> <br /> It's nice in the sense you just don't have to grab the whole 'bag' of contracts anymore.<br /> <br /> And, honestly, there were a lot of redundant contracts in the same seeming that could have been combined. In Fang and Talon, Talking with the Animal and gaining a sense of the animal really should have been combined, as an example. I would like to see, whatever contracts get presented have a fair bit of use (it's impossible to balance them all perfectly, I know I know, but in the first iteration, there were just contracts that were flat out better)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/287-wildfire","name":"Wildfire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-05T11:23:31-07:00","id":249960,"title":"","content":"One of my concerns is that Seeming Contracts can inform a fairly narrow concept of the Seeming. All of the building-focused contracts for Wizened aren't really applicable to the non-builder kiths (which is most of them). Contracts of Elements can similarly get weird when you stray into non-conventional elements. I just don't see how they add much by being associated with Seemings. I'd much prefer the space be used for more Universal Contracts which players can pick and choose from to get the character they want. As much as I love Changeling, one of my main gripes is that I found myself scraping for contracts which fit my character's concept most of the time and a lot of this was because of the need to wed most of the contracts to Seeming or Court. Since kith is going to do the heavy lifting in terms of the specific manifestation of your changes and they are being uncoupled from Seemings, I think Seeming Contracts should follow suit.<br /> <br /> Really, I suppose the common theme in what I want is the ability to have a wide range of bits to build a Changeling. Faeries are traditionally depicted as a really diverse lot and part of the joy of it to me is just how creative you can get with your concepts. I can come up with dozens of Changeling NPCs to populate a setting and have none of them be at all alike. You can be almost anything. Lost was a real improvement over Dreaming in this respect and I'd like to see the last few impediments towards really free-form building removed.<br /> <br /> Okay, I'll shut up now. Carry on. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-05T13:48:52-07:00","id":250099,"title":"","content":"Here is my own idea on the new contract system :<br /> <br /> There is no &quot;universal&quot; or &quot;seeming&quot; contracts. There is just &quot;contracts. Each contract has a power, a cost and a catch. For what would be a &quot;universal&quot; contract, that's it. For what would be a &quot;seeming&quot; contract, you add a spin on the contract for a few (or all) the seemings. One of those seeming spin can be a little stronger than the others (to make it &quot;favored&quot;), but I personally think they should all be about the same power level. Some seeming could be skipped, but I don't think there really is a need to skip one and only one all the time. Sometimes it could be more than one, sometimes there could be none missing. Also, you can never buy a contract with the seeming spin of an other seeming than yours.<br /> <br /> What we get from that is a system that reinforce some thematics and liberate the mechanics from some artificial constraints.<br /> <br /> - A changeling with no seeming can buy any contract. Their contract is just a little less powerful than a changeling with a seeming. If the seeming is a factor of the changeling's agency, the changeling with no agency does not get to put his personal spin on a contract. The contract is law and you follow it to the letter. You did not assert you individuality, so you're still just a prop in someone else's story (your keeper's).<br /> <br /> - Your seeming is the expression of your agency. You're not only a prop anymore. You have taken some control over the rules that were imposed on you. That's why you can put your own spin on your contracts; you can bend it a little in your own way. That also means you cannot &quot;fake&quot; your agency, meaning you cannot invoke a contract with the spin of an other seeming.<br /> <br /> In one of the books (I don't remember which) there was rule to shift your kith/seeming over time to something new. If at some point we allow a changeling to buy an other seeming's version of a contract, in my mind that would mean the changeling evolved and changed to that seeming first.<br /> <br /> Also, all contracts are accessible in some form, even if a contract has no spin for your particular seeming.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3816-emperorclydeiv","name":"EmperorClydeIV","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-05T14:04:24-07:00","id":250107,"title":"","content":"I like it. <br /> <br /> Bear in mind that doing it that way means that the Seeming-specific \u201cspins\u201d (which I\u2019d still call \u201cclauses\u201d) favor the Seemings that get them over the ones that don\u2019t. Beyond that, judging the \u201cbalance\u201d between the various Seemings is something of a fool\u2019s errand: attempts to do so generally involve invoking the White Room, and the whole exercise is largely rendered meaningless by the fact that no one gets to pick more than one Seeming\u2019s \u201cspin\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-05T20:22:22-07:00","id":250358,"title":"","content":"First I'd like to say I'm happy with the &quot;bag of trick&quot; approach. Only iconic powers, at whatever level needed, with less &quot;filling&quot; powers. It looks like the discreet powers will also be also more versatile (like turning into an animal will also allow you to talk to similar animals). But it also look like 5 dots powers will be more easily picked up. How would you limit that in character creation ? And during character progression, wouldn't it be more attractive to bank XP have one 5 dots power rather than three 2 dots powers (I didn't do the math for XP equivalence, but you see what I mean) ?<br /> <br /> As for Goblin contracts. As I see it, all contracts should be optionally Goblins, this option being an intermediate between Pledges and regular Contracts. So you can either buy a regular contract at regular XP cost, or a &quot;corrupted&quot; version (i.e. goblin) at reduced XP cost, or even free during some kind of bargain at the market or in the Hedge. Of course, the goblin version have a bad side effect, like having the dramatic failure result going along the success result of the contract, or some side effect especially designed for the goblin version.<br /> <br /> Just my 2 cents of course <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3648-nepher","name":"Nepher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3648_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-06T00:24:02-07:00","id":250567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EmperorClydeIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts?p=250099#post250099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here is my own idea on the new contract system :<br /> <br /> There is no &quot;universal&quot; or &quot;seeming&quot; contracts. There is just &quot;contracts. Each contract has a power, a cost and a catch. For what would be a &quot;universal&quot; contract, that's it. For what would be a &quot;seeming&quot; contract, you add a spin on the contract for a few (or all) the seemings. One of those seeming spin can be a little stronger than the others (to make it &quot;favored&quot;), but I personally think they should all be about the same power level. Some seeming could be skipped, but I don't think there really is a need to skip one and only one all the time. Sometimes it could be more than one, sometimes there could be none missing. Also, you can never buy a contract with the seeming spin of an other seeming than yours.<br /> <br /> What we get from that is a system that reinforce some thematics and liberate the mechanics from some artificial constraints.<br /> <br /> - A changeling with no seeming can buy any contract. Their contract is just a little less powerful than a changeling with a seeming. If the seeming is a factor of the changeling's agency, the changeling with no agency does not get to put his personal spin on a contract. The contract is law and you follow it to the letter. You did not assert you individuality, so you're still just a prop in someone else's story (your keeper's).<br /> <br /> - Your seeming is the expression of your agency. You're not only a prop anymore. You have taken some control over the rules that were imposed on you. That's why you can put your own spin on your contracts; you can bend it a little in your own way. That also means you cannot &quot;fake&quot; your agency, meaning you cannot invoke a contract with the spin of an other seeming.<br /> <br /> In one of the books (I don't remember which) there was rule to shift your kith/seeming over time to something new. If at some point we allow a changeling to buy an other seeming's version of a contract, in my mind that would mean the changeling evolved and changed to that seeming first.<br /> <br /> Also, all contracts are accessible in some form, even if a contract has no spin for your particular seeming.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Agree. All Changling should be able to learn all Arcadia's magic, only some Seemings could benefit more from some powers. But there is a problem with that take also - to this day Contracts were lists of powers. With &quot;it's all universal now&quot; we can only have one power per Contract - so not 6 powers for Contract of Strenght to choose for your character, only one per theme. So powers will be more... boring.<br /> <br /> But I like approche with Seeming Contracts having many &quot;Facets&quot; ( to still from <b>Forsaken</b> 2e name ), and you can buy any one you like, only it could be more costley for you. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-06T08:40:52-07:00","id":250784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EmperorClydeIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts?p=250099#post250099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here is my own idea on the new contract system :<br /> <br /> There is no &quot;universal&quot; or &quot;seeming&quot; contracts. There is just &quot;contracts. Each contract has a power, a cost and a catch. For what would be a &quot;universal&quot; contract, that's it. For what would be a &quot;seeming&quot; contract, you add a spin on the contract for a few (or all) the seemings. One of those seeming spin can be a little stronger than the others (to make it &quot;favored&quot;), but I personally think they should all be about the same power level. Some seeming could be skipped, but I don't think there really is a need to skip one and only one all the time. Sometimes it could be more than one, sometimes there could be none missing. Also, you can never buy a contract with the seeming spin of an other seeming than yours.<br /> <br /> What we get from that is a system that reinforce some thematics and liberate the mechanics from some artificial constraints.<br /> <br /> - A changeling with no seeming can buy any contract. Their contract is just a little less powerful than a changeling with a seeming. If the seeming is a factor of the changeling's agency, the changeling with no agency does not get to put his personal spin on a contract. The contract is law and you follow it to the letter. You did not assert you individuality, so you're still just a prop in someone else's story (your keeper's).<br /> <br /> - Your seeming is the expression of your agency. You're not only a prop anymore. You have taken some control over the rules that were imposed on you. That's why you can put your own spin on your contracts; you can bend it a little in your own way. That also means you cannot &quot;fake&quot; your agency, meaning you cannot invoke a contract with the spin of an other seeming.<br /> <br /> In one of the books (I don't remember which) there was rule to shift your kith/seeming over time to something new. If at some point we allow a changeling to buy an other seeming's version of a contract, in my mind that would mean the changeling evolved and changed to that seeming first.<br /> <br /> Also, all contracts are accessible in some form, even if a contract has no spin for your particular seeming.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I think there's been some misconception about what no seeming is. I really don't like the change that seems to be happening. It's always been more of a you weren't there long enough rather than a you were just let go and this change really augments a number of a characters who were designed with no seeming in mind because of the shift in tone to something that is originally a merit. One with major disadvantages tied to it. Seeming contracts should probably be flavored solely towards one seemings purview rather than an all purpose one. However I'd add a flat tax to said purview rather than per power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-06T09:46:02-07:00","id":250824,"title":"","content":"One thing that must be brought up in the Facet comparison that makes it an improper fit is that those Facets are keyed to Renown, not Auspice. This factors a few things.<br /> <br /> 1)Renown is something everyone can buy and invest in, Seemings aren't. Yes, you can buy a merit that makes it so you count as another one, but I've always had a minor feeling that's a 'pick one and settle' sort of deal. The dynamic is therefore different and more limited for players-which is fine in ways, but...well, let me make the other points.<br /> 2)Renown is a thing you buy, Seemings aren't. Now, granted, buying Renown means you get either a Moon Gift and a Shadow Gift or you get some Facets, and of course it makes those powers more potent, but the point is that you are first investing in something not inherently related to the gifts you're using-okay, I need to explain that a little better.<br /> <br /> THe point I'm getting at, with Renown, Gifts, and Facets, is that, from an EXP expenditure point of view, isn't exactly the same as buying gifts and facets, although it is related. You can just go and buy facets(barring renown qualifications), but the setup leads you to buy Renown first. It's an extraneous buy that has become very beneficial to have regardless.<br /> <br /> How that relates to seemings is that a Changeling doesn't sink EXP into other things inherently, Court Contracts aside. They just buy the Contract. When we use the Renown system as a mirror, this says a few things about EXP and power. All the Shadow Gifts are three dot powers, effectively, because Renown serves this sort of buffer state between the powers. I imagine Renown is still fairly expensive, even if Gifts and Facets aren't so much themselves. So without that diversion of Renown, Contracts either become more expensive, or the power drops, or some mixture of both(which, I'm sure, is fine for some people, as that fits Changeling). Having Seemings fill in the same place just-<br /> <br /> -....Goddamnit, I lost my train of thought.<br /> <br /> Anyways, here's where I'm going. Seeming as an underline to Contracts is pretty cool, and Facets are a good comparison to keep in mind, but I don't think we should have Facets be the absolute guiding star here. It can inform, it shouldn't direct. I think Contracts benefit a lot from having the power that seemings underline, rather than something more directly facet-y<br /> <br /> I mean, if nothing else, Werewolf has done Facets. Changeling can do something else.<br /> <br /> PS: My mind wants me to mention that DnD 4th Edition had powers similar to the entire underlining thing, so here you go.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-06T10:09:00-07:00","id":250858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>eberg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts?p=249960#post249960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of my concerns is that Seeming Contracts can inform a fairly narrow concept of the Seeming. All of the building-focused contracts for Wizened aren't really applicable to the non-builder kiths (which is most of them). Contracts of Elements can similarly get weird when you stray into non-conventional elements. I just don't see how they add much by being associated with Seemings. I'd much prefer the space be used for more Universal Contracts which players can pick and choose from to get the character they want. As much as I love Changeling, one of my main gripes is that I found myself scraping for contracts which fit my character's concept most of the time and a lot of this was because of the need to wed most of the contracts to Seeming or Court. Since kith is going to do the heavy lifting in terms of the specific manifestation of your changes and they are being uncoupled from Seemings, I think Seeming Contracts should follow suit.<br /> <br /> Really, I suppose the common theme in what I want is the ability to have a wide range of bits to build a Changeling. Faeries are traditionally depicted as a really diverse lot and part of the joy of it to me is just how creative you can get with your concepts. I can come up with dozens of Changeling NPCs to populate a setting and have none of them be at all alike. You can be almost anything. Lost was a real improvement over Dreaming in this respect and I'd like to see the last few impediments towards really free-form building removed.<br /> <br /> Okay, I'll shut up now. Carry on. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The idea would be that we could actually use the Seeming variations on Contracts to branch out and expand the ideas of Seemings. Seeing what Contract of the Shadow Cloak might mean to each of six different Seemings gives us the chance to flesh out the setting and the Seemings bit by bit with very few words.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-06T13:23:17-07:00","id":251018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts?p=250858#post250858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The idea would be that we could actually use the Seeming variations on Contracts to branch out and expand the ideas of Seemings. Seeing what Contract of the Shadow Cloak might mean to each of six different Seemings gives us the chance to flesh out the setting and the Seemings bit by bit with very few words.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds pretty cool. Conceptual stage is always tough. It is easy to project your concerns on a vague concept. Once things gel, it will be much easier to see how they work. Kind of the same problem with evaluating a system on a read-through and with actual play. Really, you won't know how it works for sure until it hits the table. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-06T14:40:20-07:00","id":251064,"title":"","content":"I think what I liked best about NLight's spew was that they gave a fluff-based reasoning for the five-dot progression structure. I'd like to see the same kind of reasoning show up for the others as well; I have a pretty vague feeling right now that Contracts are just powersets because Changeling is its own game line so of course they have their own powers. It doesn't feel like their powers are the result of a contract, or that their expression is the result of invoking a clause; they just have powers and that's it. There's no thematic weight.<br /> <br /> Anyone have ideas along this line of thought? I've been holding back on this comment for several days now hoping that I'd come up with something, but I got nothing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-07T11:04:57-07:00","id":251559,"title":"","content":"Also, if we have some version of Fang and Talon in the new edition, could we maybe stop beating around the bush and just let the freaking fairies that have wings FLY for a change? The game was oddly resistant to that idea up until now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-07T15:27:51-07:00","id":251742,"title":"","content":"As long as it stays true to the spirit of Changeling the Lost, any changes are fair game. Though I'll admit, a lot of fun was had with the &quot;catch&quot; for each contract. Ooh! What if all the contracts had different catches depending on seeming? I think that'd be better than making the contract change its effects. That'd actually be annoying, if you wanted to be a beast shapeshifter, but the Mirror Contract did something opposed to the concept envisioned by the player.<br /> <br /> Edit: I'm just saying contracts should be streamlined, or else it gets difficult keeping track of everything for players and storytellers alike. Keep it simple, you know?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":974,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","user":"MrParaduo","date":". 09-07-2014, 06:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-07T17:35:37-07:00","id":251784,"title":"","content":"Amazing idea. I am 100% behind the general concept here as well as the kith before the seeming idea in the other post. It sounds like nice upgrades to me. Where I'm not so sold is on how the XP is used regarding contracts. It is something I always felt was fuzzy in 1e (and I mean no offense to the writers) and I have concerns that it may remain the case here. Please allow me to explain, as my intent here is to openly share and hopefully help, not to criticize.<br /> <br /> Spending XP for skills make sense, as it reprensent the actual experience you gain from the time spent working on becoming better at something. No need to expand on this concept. But, contracts are... well, deals. Made long ago between two parties. Without ever having read the contract to know of its intricacies (because it was likely verbal and never written) you manage to claim yourself as eligible to receive the benefits of that deal via a technicality and you pay for it with the non-existing currency of XP?<br /> <br /> I may have completely misunderstood the concept, but that was how I read the core book so I never could understand how you suddenly came to know how to make yourself eligible and why it should cost XP to state out loud &quot;because I'm made of leaves, I should be able to do X&quot;. Or for that matter why allies couldn't just tell each other &quot;BTW, you're made of leaves. So, you're eligible.&quot; and then contracts get spread like cookies.<br /> <br /> Don't get me wrong, I love contracts. The idea is brilliant and so perfectly in tune with the spirit of Changeling: The Lost. In my games, I usually have each courts have a changeling as the role of Keeper. People who are tasked with the keeping of lore on ancient contracts and of protecting their secrets. Gaining access to contracts requires favor from a court, or a keeper willing to look away) so that you could spend time reading them and getting to know them intimately (spending time and effort = XP) so that you could eventually find the loophole allowing you to use it.<br /> <br /> But to go back to my point, here you have contracts tied to five seemings. So it becomes &quot;Yeah, I'm made of leaves, so I should be able to do X (1XP) and also, I'm pretty so really you should also let me benefit from this second aspect of this contract too (2XP) and and you know I have a primal heart, so, it makes sense that I could also do X (3XP)&quot;. From a technical standpoint looking at the possibilities I honestly adore this approach. However, as a storyteller or a player I find it difficult to maintain immersion.<br /> <br /> If I may suggest other ideas:<br /> <br /> 1 As others have, may be untying the contracts to the concept of XP or gaining them by technicality might work? Suppose, for example, that contracts aren't gained by way of being something but also of having accomplished something. Surmise, for example, that they require a price from the character. Suppose, the creator of the Vainglory contract had to abandon his only love to seal the deal, maybe today changelings who are eligible by virtue of a technicality must also pay a similar price to become party to the original arrangement? Then, entire sessions and stories might erupt from the simple need of the motley for one of their own to gain a certain ability. &quot;Guys, we need our Ogre to gain the favors of Vainglory for this plan to work so... how do we arrange for a women to fall in love with him?&quot;<br /> <br /> 2. May be the idea of the keeper (explained above) or any variation deemed more appropriate could be worked into a mechanic?<br /> <br /> Well, that turned into quite the all of text. Sorry about that and thank you for your time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3822-yiodan","name":"Yiodan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-08T00:00:24-07:00","id":252033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yiodan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts?p=251784#post251784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, that turned into quite the all of text. Sorry about that and thank you for your time.</div> </div> </div> </div>First of all, I am intrigued by your ideas and wish to subscribe to your newsletter.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yiodan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts?p=251784#post251784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spending XP for skills make sense, as it reprensent the actual experience you gain from the time spent working on becoming better at something. No need to expand on this concept. But, contracts are... well, deals. Made long ago between two parties. Without ever having read the contract to know of its intricacies (because it was likely verbal and never written) you manage to claim yourself as eligible to receive the benefits of that deal via a technicality and you pay for it with the non-existing currency of XP?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's also worth remembering that XP is also the OOC currency of &quot;the ST doesn't get to screw around with this&quot;. XP is a way for the player to define the kind of character they're playing, and that control is, while negotiated with the ST, also sacrosanct.<br /> <br /> This doesn't detract from your point, but I feel like it's the wrong direction to try to make XP expenditure have in-game meaning. It's a system for the ST to negotiate character control in return for interesting story. Trying to explain something bought with XP as &quot;spending time and effort&quot; might work in most cases, but it's an unnecessary burden for the game design.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yiodan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts?p=251784#post251784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my games, I usually have each courts have a changeling as the role of Keeper. People who are tasked with the keeping of lore on ancient contracts and of protecting their secrets. Gaining access to contracts requires favor from a court, or a keeper willing to look away) so that you could spend time reading them and getting to know them intimately (spending time and effort = XP) so that you could eventually find the loophole allowing you to use it.<br /> <br /> But to go back to my point, here you have contracts tied to five seemings. So it becomes &quot;Yeah, I'm made of leaves, so I should be able to do X (1XP) and also, I'm pretty so really you should also let me benefit from this second aspect of this contract too (2XP) and and you know I have a primal heart, so, it makes sense that I could also do X (3XP)&quot;. From a technical standpoint looking at the possibilities I honestly adore this approach. However, as a storyteller or a player I find it difficult to maintain immersion.<br /> <br /> If I may suggest other ideas:<br /> <br /> 1 As others have, may be untying the contracts to the concept of XP or gaining them by technicality might work? Suppose, for example, that contracts aren't gained by way of being something but also of having accomplished something. Surmise, for example, that they require a price from the character. Suppose, the creator of the Vainglory contract had to abandon his only love to seal the deal, maybe today changelings who are eligible by virtue of a technicality must also pay a similar price to become party to the original arrangement? Then, entire sessions and stories might erupt from the simple need of the motley for one of their own to gain a certain ability. &quot;Guys, we need our Ogre to gain the favors of Vainglory for this plan to work so... how do we arrange for a women to fall in love with him?&quot;<br /> <br /> 2. May be the idea of the keeper (explained above) or any variation deemed more appropriate could be worked into a mechanic?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm a little uncomfortable with the idea that the overwhelming majority of Changeling powers are loopholes granting access. Simplifying it a smidge, I'd rather go with a basic ritual required to become a signatory of the contract: maybe for the Contract of Smoke you have to spend ten minutes in a smoke-filled room; it's not the doing-it that makes you a signatory, but rather the doing-it-with-the-intention-of-learning-Smoke. I dunno. Not really happy with that interpretation.<br /> <br /> Still, I really like your approach. It fits in with MrParaduo's idea of requiring different Catches for different Seemings, too. (The problem with that idea being that it's too much fluff for no real crunch.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-08T04:30:28-07:00","id":252183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts?p=252033#post252033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> First of all, I am intrigued by your ideas and wish to subscribe to your newsletter.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> It's also worth remembering that XP is also the OOC currency of &quot;the ST doesn't get to screw around with this&quot;. XP is a way for the player to define the kind of character they're playing, and that control is, while negotiated with the ST, also sacrosanct.<br /> <br /> This doesn't detract from your point, but I feel like it's the wrong direction to try to make XP expenditure have in-game meaning. It's a system for the ST to negotiate character control in return for interesting story. Trying to explain something bought with XP as &quot;spending time and effort&quot; might work in most cases, but it's an unnecessary burden for the game design.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I'm a little uncomfortable with the idea that the overwhelming majority of Changeling powers are loopholes granting access. Simplifying it a smidge, I'd rather go with a basic ritual required to become a signatory of the contract: maybe for the Contract of Smoke you have to spend ten minutes in a smoke-filled room; it's not the doing-it that makes you a signatory, but rather the doing-it-with-the-intention-of-learning-Smoke. I dunno. Not really happy with that interpretation.<br /> <br /> Still, I really like your approach. It fits in with MrParaduo's idea of requiring different Catches for different Seemings, too. (The problem with that idea being that it's too much fluff for no real crunch.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! I'll let you know if I ever start a newsletter <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> And I understand/agree with all of your points. I don't have a perfect solution yet, but I figured it worth a shot to mention the concern. At worst, it can be an interesting topic to discuss at best it gives the team food for thought.<br /> <br /> The ritual sounds like a great idea BTW, but again my issue points its head. What's to stop all members of a Motley to be in the smoke-filled room at the same time and all gain a shiny new power? Rinse, repeat, with all the powers in the book? Because the only limitation is an OOC currency the characters themselves have no reason not to do it. Especially people of Autumn who may not see an alternative if they want to be ready to fight the True Fay.<br /> <br /> New idea, let me know what you think. Could the XP represent memories? In exchange for eligibility of this contract, I give up the memory of the first time I ate apple pie at my grandmother's house it was the best I ever had. To Lost, giving up memories of this sort would be something to think about twice.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3822-yiodan","name":"Yiodan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-08T13:37:36-07:00","id":252622,"title":"","content":"I think it'd also be important to give examples on how changelings acquire new contracts. A lot of players (including me) had trouble explaining them. Are they like arcane knowledge that you need to study? Slips of dream-paper you sign onto? Or are they more bound by your personality, your character gaining them instinctively as they lean towards the contract's core tenants and ideals? If you're buying them, what does a contract look like? Or is it just a wink and a handshake from seller to buyer?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-08T13:55:09-07:00","id":252639,"title":"","content":"There's something ironic about how the flavor behind earning powers sometimes hampers it. Does that sound like gibberish?<br /> <br /> If you want to broker a deal with Fire in Changeling or hunt down and strongarm a spirit into teaching you a Gift in Werewolf, that whole event, which can practically eat up a lot of (awesomely spent) time in a session kind of feels like payment itself - to then have xp costs on top of it can be so frustrating, especially since an 'earned' power isn't any mechanically stronger than one given after a time skip or level-up cutaway, or such.<br /> <br /> Changeling's flavor always makes it sound to me like your character would not learn any non-court contracts once they are back in the mundane world unless they are in serious danger from low clarity and tapped into that dangerous, enchanting undercurrent of an otherworld... Which is of course just silly.<br /> <br /> Having a load of different ways to earn contracts is important so players aren't hampered, but there is such a disconnect from the story for some as opposed to others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-08T14:47:20-07:00","id":252675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts?p=252622#post252622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it'd also be important to give examples on how changelings acquire new contracts. A lot of players (including me) had trouble explaining them. Are they like arcane knowledge that you need to study? Slips of dream-paper you sign onto? Or are they more bound by your personality, your character gaining them instinctively as they lean towards the contract's core tenants and ideals? If you're buying them, what does a contract look like? Or is it just a wink and a handshake from seller to buyer?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's some short fiction before one of the chapters that I think shows it pretty well, a fireheart is trying to learn a clause of fleeting spring so the spring courtier who's helping him out opens a window (so spring can be present as a witness) and he lights a fire (another witness, presumably for his kith) and he cuts his hand on a rose, bleeds into the fire and makes a formal request. I think that's the kind of thing that can be described in a short scene for more fluff and flavor minded people without impeding the game. That said, it'd be nice to see at least the general idea behind the process explained in the book for storytellers would be kind of nice, I may have missed it but I don't know that there were any instances where actually gaining a contract was aknowledged outside of that one fiction bit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/807-arcadianawakened","name":"ArcadianAwakened","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-08T15:11:51-07:00","id":252690,"title":"","content":"Rites of Spring, Third Chapter opening fiction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-08T15:19:40-07:00","id":252694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcadianAwakened</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts?p=252675#post252675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's some short fiction before one of the chapters that I think shows it pretty well, a fireheart is trying to learn a clause of fleeting spring so the spring courtier who's helping him out opens a window (so spring can be present as a witness) and he lights a fire (another witness, presumably for his kith) and he cuts his hand on a rose, bleeds into the fire and makes a formal request. I think that's the kind of thing that can be described in a short scene for more fluff and flavor minded people without impeding the game. That said, it'd be nice to see at least the general idea behind the process explained in the book for storytellers would be kind of nice, I may have missed it but I don't know that there were any instances where actually gaining a contract was aknowledged outside of that one fiction bit.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts?p=252690#post252690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rites of Spring, Third Chapter opening fiction.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, both of you. I seem to have missed this and it's exactly the sort of concrete example I was looking for.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Barbrarilen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts?p=252639#post252639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's something ironic about how the flavor behind earning powers sometimes hampers it. Does that sound like gibberish?<br /> <br /> If you want to broker a deal with Fire in Changeling or hunt down and strongarm a spirit into teaching you a Gift in Werewolf, that whole event, which can practically eat up a lot of (awesomely spent) time in a session kind of feels like payment itself - to then have xp costs on top of it can be so frustrating, especially since an 'earned' power isn't any mechanically stronger than one given after a time skip or level-up cutaway, or such.<br /> <br /> Having a load of different ways to earn contracts is important so players aren't hampered, but there is such a disconnect from the story for some as opposed to others.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very much agreed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3822-yiodan","name":"Yiodan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-08T15:33:47-07:00","id":252700,"title":"","content":"I know there's a section in Rites of Spring, but it isn't very big. Just wanted more elaboration is all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-08T15:59:05-07:00","id":252712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Barbrarilen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts?p=252639#post252639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's something ironic about how the flavor behind earning powers sometimes hampers it. Does that sound like gibberish?<br /> <br /> If you want to broker a deal with Fire in Changeling or hunt down and strongarm a spirit into teaching you a Gift in Werewolf, that whole event, which can practically eat up a lot of (awesomely spent) time in a session kind of feels like payment itself - to then have xp costs on top of it can be so frustrating, especially since an 'earned' power isn't any mechanically stronger than one given after a time skip or level-up cutaway, or such.<br /> <br /> Changeling's flavor always makes it sound to me like your character would not learn any non-court contracts once they are back in the mundane world unless they are in serious danger from low clarity and tapped into that dangerous, enchanting undercurrent of an otherworld... Which is of course just silly.<br /> <br /> Having a load of different ways to earn contracts is important so players aren't hampered, but there is such a disconnect from the story for some as opposed to others.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see a huge need for there to be an in-game session dedicated to learning it, but I do think there should be an in-game <i>explanation</i>. It doesn't even have to be a great explanation, but it should reinforce the themes. &quot;I hunted down the appropriate spirit and learned the Gift of Whatsit&quot; can happen off-screen, by my lights, and that's fine. Or &quot;I spent some time off-screen to learn about the Death Arcanum so now I have a dot in it.&quot; To me, it's the standard &quot;so when did the adventurer go to the bathroom, exactly?&quot; There isn't some dungeon-crawler pixie dust that makes them immune to the need to defecate; it's just something that happened off-screen.<br /> <br /> To me, XP expenditure is just &quot;I have sealed this as part of my character.&quot; There's a difference between buying the Striking Looks merit and using a power to achieve the same result; in the former case, the ST can't touch it. In the latter case, the ST might dispel the Life spell or invalidate the Contract's effect or whatever. Similarly, if you get a bunch of Changelings who all sit in a room and learn about Smoke, but they don't spend XP to buy the Contract on their sheet, I'd find that grounds to story hook that into that having random stuff happen to make them lose access to those powers too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-08T16:29:12-07:00","id":252749,"title":"","content":"I'm not talking about explaining how it works, I'm talking about the narrative presentation. How do you present the existence of contracts ingame? If you were writing a book using the changeling setting, how would the characters learn about contracts? How would you describe the process in a narrative?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-08T23:50:13-07:00","id":253083,"title":"","content":"Learning about contracts usually involves a mentor or reading. Like an attorney's office with the world, I imagine changelings have all sorts of 'legal documents' that explain the set up for a Contract.<br /> <br /> Of course, the thing of the matter is that Contracts are a matter of speaking though the clauses of that contract. A lot of the Wyrd Sorcery(I'm just borrowing the term guys) stuff you see in fairy tales is actually the articulation and exploration of a Contract. Grimoires are books of laws for changelings, each spell the signing of it. But I imagine it's taught by either reading the law books or learning it from a teacher.<br /> <br /> Enacting Contracts is something akin to dialing the phone number of the universe and calling it to fulfill its' dues, with the glamour or catch filling in for the change you plug into the machine.<br /> <br /> No...that metaphor's not quite right. Certainly a short story (Lost 1st Edition, Chapter Two opening story) shows that a changeling thought to the wall, so sure, it's true in a sense. But Contracts are the little brothers of Titles, same as Pledges are(I'm not sure where to place Pledges and Contracts on the scales). By signing the Contract, the aspect and the Changeling are kind of one,within the terms defined, much like a Stranger is his domain. Glamour and Catches just provide the momentary wiring, affording changelings some distance and identity by having the connection not all be 'on'. Pledges are always 'on', so long as it's defined so.<br /> <br /> Maybe when the other side talks back, that's all just the changeling. I dunno, somewhere between the payphone and the wiring metaphors is the truth.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-09T00:08:00-07:00","id":253088,"title":"","content":"Hrm. Sort of tangential, and possibly off-topic: wtf is the Wyrd? I scanned through the corebook's description of the Advantage, but it makes it seem like a character attribute rather than a property of the universe, which means I'm probably looking in the wrong place. (The un-tangential part: I'm trying to imagine <i>where</i> Arcane's metaphorical law books actually are, and the answer that leapt to mind was &quot;the Wyrd&quot;.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-09T00:21:55-07:00","id":253100,"title":"","content":"1)No, I mean Freeholds probably collect law books. Of course, those look like spellbooks.<br /> <br /> ...Course, it makes sense one can intuit them by connection to the Wyrd, but that's....fun. Namely because!<br /> <br /> 2)The Wyrd is a thing all Fae have, and the more connected to it they are, the more powerful they get.<br /> <br /> Wyrd is....the simplest way to put it is that it is that it's connections. It is a active, if not living, force of connection between everything. THe reason the Self can have a sense of the Other is because of the Wyrd. Fire can burn you because of the Wyrd. You can command fire to dance when you invoke the Cotnract because of the Wyrd.<br /> <br /> Sound broad and vague? That's because it is. The Wyrd is the force of metaphor and simile, it is the power in the words 'like' and 'as'. It's the force of karma, of the sense that actions have consequences. It is the analogy and narrative. The Wyrd is every bridge to any and all linked concepts. It is, by necessity, a lot of things and abstract.<br /> <br /> The easiest way to put it? The Wyrd is the narrative. Not <i>just </i> the Storyteller and the players, but the inspiration that comes to them as well.<br /> <br /> Easiest, but not the most useful.<br /> <br /> Anyways, that's why intuiting a Contract in the Wyrd is hard. It's like figuring out the shape of the elephant by only using your hands.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Actually, if I had to pick another word beyond connections, it'd be context. Which is actually pretty much the same thing, so its a force of connections, the power of bridges.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 09-09-2014, 03:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-09T02:25:59-07:00","id":253165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts?p=248225#post248225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> In our experience, yes, it's the five dot structure. If, as a developer, you come up with an interesting idea for a power that you feel really warrants inclusion, the onus is then on you to craft four other powers. For example, Vampire's gone through tons of editions. None of the core Disciplines have gone without any sort of change, because some of the powers rendered each other redundant, were boring, or felt thematically out of place. But there are certainly powers we know we want vampires to have. After over 20 years, we're still feeling them out and tinkering with them in order to make that five dot progression feel right. If we're still struggling with that after 20 years and dozens of writers, the structure is probably to blame, yes.</div> </div> </div> </div> I really don't mind forgetting the 5-dots system, but I really have a question: If the 5-dot system is a design problem because you have to come up with 5 powers, why change it with a system where you have to design 6 different variations of the same power? I mean, in theory you'd run into the same problems designing 6 variations of the same contract (redundancy, theme, etc) than creating 5 tiered powers. Plus, you'd have to change the testing process to accommodate the fact (testing the different contracts in different seeming combinations so no degenerate combinations occur or no Seeming gets all the boring, out-of-place contracts).<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3830-dregotim","name":"dregotim","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-09T02:28:44-07:00","id":253169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dregotim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts?p=253165#post253165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I really don't mind forgetting the 5-dots system, but I really have a question: If the 5-dot system is a design problem because you have to come up with 5 powers, why change it with a system where you have to design 6 different variations of the same power? I mean, in theory you'd run into the same problems designing 6 variations of the same contract (redundancy, theme, etc) than creating 5 tiered powers. Plus, you'd have to change the testing process to accommodate the fact (testing the different contracts in different seeming combinations so no degenerate combinations occur or no Seeming gets all the boring, out-of-place contracts).<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>This is actually why we have Seeming Contracts and Universal Contracts. Some will make sense one way, some the other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-09T03:19:31-07:00","id":253185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts?p=253169#post253169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is actually why we have Seeming Contracts and Universal Contracts. Some will make sense one way, some the other.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok. And if your Seeming Contract is boring/redundant, you can still access the cool parts paying a bit more, you you're not stuck with your Seeming version. It gives the payers options and does not constraints.<br /> <br /> It it looks really good on paper. Now I really want to see the implementation.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3830-dregotim","name":"dregotim","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-09T04:57:22-07:00","id":253232,"title":"","content":"Its the power of Like and As? Badass, Arcane <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-09T08:51:18-07:00","id":253319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dregotim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts?p=253185#post253185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ok. And if your Seeming Contract is boring/redundant, you can still access the cool parts paying a bit more, you you're not stuck with your Seeming version. It gives the payers options and does not constraints.<br /> <br /> It it looks really good on paper. Now I really want to see the implementation.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'd rather they just be straight forward and not confuse the players with several variations of rules depending on seeming. It'd slow the game to a crawl if you had to explain why your fairest's contract of beasts is different to the ogre's, when they're both the same level. Besides, limitations are what make the game fun and challenging. It's much more rewarding to use a contract smartly over an opponent who has the same contract to prove your superior skill and implementation of its powers, regardless of kith or seeming.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-09T08:54:28-07:00","id":253321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Barbrarilen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts?p=253232#post253232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its the power of Like and As? Badass, Arcane <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Badass, sure. Useful?<br /> <br /> Eh, something that involved a quick reread and deeper thought process would have been better. I have a very pretty description up there, but I'd suggest its' usefulness as a concrete definition is lacking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-09T09:43:00-07:00","id":253373,"title":"","content":"The clarification is helpful; thanks. I'm going to set this on the backburner and let it stew for a while. *mumbles something about toil and trouble*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-09T09:58:59-07:00","id":253384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts?p=253321#post253321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Badass, sure. Useful?<br /> <br /> Eh, something that involved a quick reread and deeper thought process would have been better. I have a very pretty description up there, but I'd suggest its' usefulness as a concrete definition is lacking.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interpretation/concept is still fluff - which obviously has intrinsic value - but concrete definitions can rob us of options? Don't lose the forest for a really handsome tree <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-09T11:07:40-07:00","id":253476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts?p=248552#post248552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Throwing out structure just seems like an open invite for early power creep and the &quot;yeah, whatever, let's let them do this&quot; like Gifts from Apocalypse that stray off to unthematic regions.</div> </div> </div> </div>This actually <i>is</i> a risk, I think. I noticed there was a certain degree of ... awkwardness in nDemon's non-tiered abilities; powers that were really too strong or too weak being shoeorned into the same box; which kind of gave a sense that their powers were more, well <i>powerful</i> than anything else they could buy. If an ability was to &quot;compete&quot; for our attention, it almost <i>needed </i>to be too powerful.<br /> <br /> I think this is nicely solved by keeping the dot rating without requiring each Contract fit into a matching set of five, though, that's a really excellent idea.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts?p=248552#post248552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Skipping levels in the progression also stunts the curve. Speaking as a player rather than a GM, knowing how to use the low level abilities effectively sets you up for applications of the higher end. Jumping right into the deep end of a contract will just leave you to drown in your own ideas, wondering &quot;why did I pick this again?&quot; Your mileage may vary, but I'm drawing on my experiences specifically with Reflections. It goes somewhere, and I'd be in unfamiliar waters if I jumped right into reaching through a reflective surface to grab the knife in my bathroom's toothbrush holder if I hadn't gone through the experience of grabbing my television and rewinding to find out how the hell I ended up on my couch when I was left for dead in the Hedge the night before.<br /> <br /> [...]<br /> <br /> Divorcing the progressive structure cheats the deal. You don't learn your way around using the concept creatively (which many clauses need to be utilized as more than parlor tricks). You just jump right in and say &quot;Ha! I'm a giant fireball! FEAR ME!&quot; without having any progression up to that point that proves to the concept that you'll even know WTF you're doing. See above about the curve. You start the promise, the Contract, and you fulfill your end of the bargain through application, and get paid with access to more and greater.<br /> <br /> Ok. That's my spew for now. I'll get the mop.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the biggest issue with this is ... what if I don't <i>want </i>lower levels? What if they don't fit my character?<br /> <br /> If my starting concept is &quot;I'm a giant fireball!&quot;, does it really make sense to force me to buy &quot;pyrokinesis&quot; or &quot;see infrared&quot; before &quot;they can't catch you if you're on fire!&quot;? I might decide I want those <i>later</i>, but then again, I might decide I want to fly instead. Why not at least extend the option?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enokh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts?p=248666#post248666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Minor point of contention, <b>game balance between lines isn't a thing at all</b>. On purpose. Not because they want unbalance, but because it isn't a concern. As....DaveB, I think, said: They aren't going to make Spirit Arcana weaker so that Werewolves can be the best at Spiriting. They're going to make Spirit as strong as the other Arcana.<br /> <br /> No balance between lines, simply interaction.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is, in fact, a thing.<br /> <br /> The designers don't worry about interfering with the<i> themes and mechanics</i> of other games, yes, because those are separate tools in the toolbox you can pick up or put down as you wish. But they all share the same core rules for Merits, Attributes, Skills, etc. etc. Abilities are (in theory) balanced with those options, and thus remain compatible with any other content for those same core rules.<br /> <br /> No interaction between lines, simply balance.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yiodan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts?p=251784#post251784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I may have completely misunderstood the concept, but that was how I read the core book so I never could understand how you suddenly came to know how to make yourself eligible and why it should cost XP to state out loud &quot;because I'm made of leaves, I should be able to do X&quot;. Or for that matter why allies couldn't just tell each other &quot;BTW, you're made of leaves. So, you're eligible.&quot; and then contracts get spread like cookies.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I understand it, that would be the remaining niche of Goblin Contracts, now you can buy regular Contracts out of order:<br /> <br /> A regular Contract is, essentially, a tried-and-tested Goblin Contract; it's reliable, so you have to pay XP. Much like you have to buy the Resources Merit to, say, own a shop.<br /> <br /> But yes, you <i>can </i>just make one up on the fly. If you have the right skillset. It will be hard, and costly, and most importantly <i>unreliable - </i>but you can do it, in a pinch. That would be, metaphorically, selling some junk to get enough money to pay the rent - you have to find a buyer, and you can't do this every month, but you get a pile of cash with the right Availability and you can spend it, regardless of where it came from.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":877,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","user":"MugaSofer","date":". 09-09-2014, 02:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","name":"MugaSofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar877_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-09T15:43:48-07:00","id":253639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MugaSofer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts?p=253476#post253476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is, in fact, a thing.<br /> <br /> The designers don't worry about interfering with the<i> themes and mechanics</i> of other games, yes, because those are separate tools in the toolbox you can pick up or put down as you wish. But they all share the same core rules for Merits, Attributes, Skills, etc. etc. Abilities are (in theory) balanced with those options, and thus remain compatible with any other content for those same core rules.<br /> <br /> No interaction between lines, simply balance.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Eh. Having been on most major design discussions in the past few years, including those for God-Machine, Vampire, Werewolf, Mage, Promethean, Changeling, Beast, and Demon, I assure you this is a tertiary concern at best. A lot of times someone will say, &quot;This thing and balance between lines!&quot; and inevitably, someone developing will butt in and respond, &quot;But other things more important to the design...&quot; <br /> <br /> I can't remember the last major change or tweak we've made in the consideration of crossover balance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-09T16:03:17-07:00","id":253649,"title":"","content":"I guess I don't really want balance between the lines. After all, in my games, we have humans as well as mages, and there's no balance there whatsoever. What I do enjoy is support for crossover. I like the idea of using every nWoD core book and supplement as modular content that can be added onto another game. Demon is particularly great at this, as it mentions the other lines frequently, and includes a few powers that can interact with the Otherworlds in the rest of the WoD gamelines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-09T17:10:44-07:00","id":253679,"title":"","content":"If each Contract is a thing unto itself, could there be benefits to learning Contracts linked by a common theme? IE, if someone learns three Contracts that deal with creating/manipulating weather, could they be used simultaneously, or at a bonus?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-09T17:54:10-07:00","id":253699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shkspr1048</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts?p=253679#post253679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If each Contract is a thing unto itself, could there be benefits to learning Contracts linked by a common theme? IE, if someone learns three Contracts that deal with creating/manipulating weather, could they be used simultaneously, or at a bonus?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm. My only concern with this is, we'd have to tie them hard to make it really work with any reasonable reliability. That would mean like a keyword system or something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-09T18:13:29-07:00","id":253734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts?p=253699#post253699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hm. My only concern with this is, we'd have to tie them hard to make it really work with any reasonable reliability. That would mean like a keyword system or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>That said, it sounds like something that might be workable in a supplement as new type of power/bonus. Use it to evoke those more sorcerous ideas that occasionally get tapped into, like the curse from the fiction at the start of Dancers in the Dusk Chapter Two.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-09T20:57:40-07:00","id":253795,"title":"","content":"I do sort of like that idea. It fits into the gameplay concept (as I understand it) that the Lost generally want to rig the game in their favor, and are usually going to tip every potential scale to their benefit in order to make that happen. It wouldn't even need to be a *huge* benefit; maybe you get a bonus to Contract activation rolls if you have related Contracts active, or maybe there's a cost break, or maybe the contracts enjoy multiplicative synergy or something (though that would be hella difficult to balance).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-09T21:37:51-07:00","id":253819,"title":"","content":"I like the idea of being able to connect Contracts in some way. Hmm... This might be too subtle, problematic, exploitable, or produce some sort of perverse incentive that's not yet occurred to me, but perhaps some allowance for a Changeling to use multiple Contracts at once, only if simultaneously fulfilling all of their Catches. For hard mode, only if the means of fulfilling one is the same as fulfilling the rest.*<br /> <br /> Easy ones might just have identical Catches,** combinations that would be overly powerful can have mutually exclusive Catches or ones that depend on incredibly creative lawyering.*** To prevent potential abuse, one caveat might be that it works just fine the first time a particular method is used to creatively combine Contracts. Trying to repeat the exact same thing no longer has that inventive spark to it: the Wyrd won't sanction it and may visit some misfortune on one who tries.<br /> <br /> Again, not sure how well this would actually work out; might be a lot of work for not a lot of payout. And it might place demands too stringent on what Catches can be, instead of just letting them be something that suits the Contract.<br /> <br /> * e.g. If the Catch for one contract is wearing something meant to keep one warm and another is wearing something red, simultaneously using both would require something red that's meant to keep one warm<br /> ** I'm admittedly not crazy about this notion. I like having lots of diversity in Catches. Aside from that, I like the Catch to be tailored to the Clause in 1e. I'd like that to be even more true, if Contracts are becoming more robust.<br /> *** I'm thinking of the sorts of incredibly dubious requirements a lot of faerie curses/blessings seem to carry that nonetheless get dramatically fulfilled through creative interpretation. Like Stardust's 'only when the moon loses her daughter in a week when two Mondays come together' deal.<br /> <br /> Ah, unrelated to this current line of thought. For Seeming Contracts, will each &quot;Clause&quot; have its own Catch, or will they all be linked by a common Catch? Especially if the idea is that the different &quot;Clauses&quot; will help to characterize the different Seemings, different Catches would help to add even more personality, so that'd certainly be my preference. On a related note, might Contracts potentially have multiple Catches? Or is the idea that Catches will have a brainspew of their own?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":"also, Wyrd not Wyld. 09-10-2014, 01:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-10T03:55:57-07:00","id":253958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts?p=253639#post253639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Eh. Having been on most major design discussions in the past few years, including those for God-Machine, Vampire, Werewolf, Mage, Promethean, Changeling, Beast, and Demon, I assure you this is a tertiary concern at best. A lot of times someone will say, &quot;This thing and balance between lines!&quot; and inevitably, someone developing will butt in and respond, &quot;But other things more important to the design...&quot;<br /> <br /> I can't remember the last major change or tweak we've made in the consideration of crossover balance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, indeed. As long as it's balanced within the core rules - no one-dot Contracts that grant +5 Strength or something - then it should be balanced with the other lines.<br /> <br /> And if it isn't, that means there's a problem with that line, not Changeling.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts?p=253819#post253819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, unrelated to this current line of thought. For Seeming Contracts, will each &quot;Clause&quot; have its own Catch, or will they all be linked by a common Catch? Especially if the idea is that the different &quot;Clauses&quot; will help to characterize the different Seemings, different Catches would help to add even more personality, so that'd certainly be my preference. On a related note, might Contracts potentially have multiple Catches? Or is the idea that Catches will have a brainspew of their own?</div> </div> </div> </div>... you know, looking at it, a lot of the differences in the example - which, OK, is off the cuff, but still - look a <i>lot</i> like Catches. Food for thought.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":877,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","user":"MugaSofer","date":". 09-10-2014, 06:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","name":"MugaSofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar877_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-11T10:58:00-07:00","id":254379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts?p=253699#post253699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hm. My only concern with this is, we'd have to tie them hard to make it really work with any reasonable reliability. That would mean like a keyword system or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>How about cribbing from Promethean, and having Contracts placed under general headings, with each heading covering several Contracts of various levels? For instance, your Contracts of Fog, Storms, and what all else could fit under 'Contracts of Weather'. Add a Text Box saying that some Contracts might reasonably fall under several headings, and to discuss such matters with the Storyteller, and there you are!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-11T16:10:04-07:00","id":254733,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shkspr1048</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts?p=254379#post254379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about cribbing from Promethean, and having Contracts placed under general headings, with each heading covering several Contracts of various levels? For instance, your Contracts of Fog, Storms, and what all else could fit under 'Contracts of Weather'. Add a Text Box saying that some Contracts might reasonably fall under several headings, and to discuss such matters with the Storyteller, and there you are!</div> </div> </div> </div>No, please don't. We already have oaths and vows. We don't need to complicate the contract mechanics more than MtAw arcana. If you want to make a system of wyrd ritual magic, fine. That's totally okay. But leave my contracts alone. &gt;:3","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-13T10:53:00-07:00","id":256143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts?p=254733#post254733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, please don't. We already have oaths and vows. We don't need to complicate the contract mechanics more than MtAw arcana. If you want to make a system of wyrd ritual magic, fine. That's totally okay. But leave my contracts alone. &gt;:3</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, now I'm lost. How is the Promethean Transmutation system complicated?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-13T11:38:51-07:00","id":256173,"title":"","content":"The problem is more that listing things inherently together limits and constrains the contracts you make. The idea behind the durrent design is to be freeing, and the contract categories create constraints that aren't helpful.<br /> <br /> This is why the idea, if it is to be pursued, would work well in a supplement as an alternative power/benefit time. You can list those powers/benefits, include prerequisites, and then give either the constant benefit or the large magic-y thing. This leaves contracts the room to be open and free and still explore the ideas that multiple contracts buys into.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-13T12:06:03-07:00","id":256179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shkspr1048</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts?p=256143#post256143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, now I'm lost. How is the Promethean Transmutation system complicated?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm just saying that there's nothing wrong with the 5 tier system. Why fix what isn't broken? Where it would get complicated is transitioning players from CtL v1 into a system that's too different from the original. You need to be slow and steady with this kind of change, you know?<br /> <br /> Besides, it might feel like we're stealing Promethean's thunder (pun not intended) if we copy off their unique form of power mechanics. Or hell, maybe it's just me. I dunno. :/","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":974,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","user":"MrParaduo","date":". 09-13-2014, 03:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-13T17:08:06-07:00","id":256369,"title":"","content":"First, the \u201cwhy fix what isn\u2019t broken?\u201d thing has already been addressed: the developers have stated that they consider the five-tier system to be broken, as well as why. The borrowing of Promethean\u2019s \u201ccategories\u201d approach is an attempt by a fan to reintroduce some of the strengths of the five-tier system without reintroducng its drawbacks. Second, Promethean is apparently going to be moving away from the way its Transmutations were set up in 2e; though I don't know what will be replacing it yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-13T17:47:05-07:00","id":256385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts?p=256369#post256369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First, the \u201cwhy fix what isn\u2019t broken?\u201d thing has already been addressed: the developers have stated that they consider the five-tier system to be broken, as well as why. The borrowing of Promethean\u2019s \u201ccategories\u201d approach is an attempt by a fan to reintroduce some of the strengths of the five-tier system without reintroducng its drawbacks. Second, Promethean is apparently going to be moving away from the way its Transmutations were set up in 2e; though I don't know what will be replacing it yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>...Point taken. Fair enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T02:22:06-08:00","id":304307,"title":"","content":"Sorry for the unholy necromancy, but I remebered this recently when trying to find an appropiate Contract for a Changelling character:<br /> <br /> Could we have an actual <i>create stuff</i> Contract? Artifice is mostly about making things don't work (and a bit of jury-rigging) and the other Affinity Contracts of the Wizened don't fit the concept of tinkerer and builder that a lot of fairy tales have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-08T01:24:05-08:00","id":306466,"title":"","content":"Where are we on the matter of double kith? Will it show up again?<br /> <br /> I hope it will, it can lead to some pretty unique characters, like Woodblood + <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Palewraith that leads to a Ghost Orchid theme, a ghastly flower hiding deep in the dark woods. It also helps making thematic gentry, like a japanese inspired lord with his private bunraku puppet theatre, where every puppet has a role: the warrior, the dancer, the thief; all of them manequins, but also a second kith.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4261-donpapillon","name":"donpapillon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4261_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-08T04:24:56-08:00","id":306546,"title":"","content":"I think that's the matter for 2.0 Seeming/Kith thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-08T08:38:33-08:00","id":306686,"title":"","content":"So rather than have dual-kith to represent those themes, instead you'd have, for example, 3 changelings with the manequin Kiths but each with a different seeming; a Darkling for the thief, a Fairest for the dancer, and an Ogre for the warrior, or something like that. I think I like this system a lot. I'm definitely looking forward to Changeling 2.0","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2291-gwyn-chan-r-gwyll","name":"Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-09T03:56:26-08:00","id":307322,"title":"","content":"You bet, it makes Changeling ever more flexible than before.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-09T11:03:59-08:00","id":307612,"title":"","content":"I'm not grasping what is being said. The one thing I would not want to see is a more complex system. I've experienced in game time that rules as they are take up enough time. Anymore complex and they can take over a game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4135-blue-thomas","name":"Blue Thomas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4135_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-10T00:42:19-08:00","id":307956,"title":"","content":"It's not complex, it just gives more flexibility.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-10T08:10:50-08:00","id":308222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blue Thomas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts?p=307612#post307612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not grasping what is being said. The one thing I would not want to see is a more complex system. I've experienced in game time that rules as they are take up enough time. Anymore complex and they can take over a game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would you clarify your points of confusion? Those of us who feel what's being said makes sense may be able to help it click for you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-10T09:11:31-08:00","id":308248,"title":"","content":"Are you going to include Goblin Vows too? I find them interesting as an open, quick, versatile yet costly system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-10T13:07:15-08:00","id":308476,"title":"","content":"Okay, so you mentioned contract creation will be easier. Can you go into detail about that?<br /> <br /> Seeing how Changelings are all about constructing vows, pledges and such from scratch, I can't see why contract weaving/crafting/smithing has to be so unreachable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4261-donpapillon","name":"donpapillon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4261_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-11T04:26:06-08:00","id":308936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts?p=308222#post308222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Would you clarify your points of confusion? Those of us who feel what's being said makes sense may be able to help it click for you.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> all if it really. but this esp:<br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Seeming Contracts </b></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Seeming Contracts will be very broad Contracts that have multiple flavors, by Seeming. When you purchase one for its level in Experiences (so a level 4 costs 4), you get your Seeming's manifestation of it. For an Experience each, you can unlock other Seemings. If your Seeming isn't represented on the Contract (most will have 5, not 6), then if you want that Contract, you have to pay the extra Experience to unlock a different Seeming's manifestation when you pick it up.<br /> <br /> For me, what I would really like to see are the contracts being more practical and more in line with concepts. For instance, Contracts of Darkness is really more about fear. So just call it contracts of fear and make one really concerning darkness. <br /> Another example, Contracts of the Forge (first dot) is too specific and in my opinion destracts from the fun of the game (not to mention that it contradicts itself. <br /> Also needed real bad are the holes left in the game. example: why don't darklings have the ability to see in the dark???</span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4135-blue-thomas","name":"Blue Thomas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4135_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-11T09:51:20-08:00","id":309243,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure that clarifies much.<br /> <br /> The Seeming Contract idea you wrote is the basic idea, though this is so early in the process that many aspects of it are likely to be tweaked (that's the whole point of the thread). Seeming Contracts will not just be, &quot;Contracts that one Seeming has an Affinity for,&quot; but in general, &quot;Contracts with Seeming variations based on Seemings.&quot;<br /> <br /> Refocusing the Contracts to cover specific things is an entirely separate matter. That's why the currently stated concept is to get Changelings off the 1-5 list style powers. Contracts will be ranked, but individual powers that don't come in set lists. This means any perceived &quot;hole&quot; in capabilities can be handled via making a new Contract.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-11T10:00:28-08:00","id":309251,"title":"","content":"So basically the idea of &quot;Seeming Contracts&quot; is that they are contracts that 5 of the 6 Seemings have an affinity for. If you are one of those 5, you get the basic ability of the Contract, but then you also get a bonus which is based on your seeming. You can buy the bonus of another seeming for a second dot. If you're the one Seeming not on the list, then you have to pay extra, but get to pick which seeming bonus you get from the contract. <br /> <br /> The example on the first page shows roughly how this would go down in practice, with different Seemings &quot;take&quot; on the basic idea of &quot;strength&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2291-gwyn-chan-r-gwyll","name":"Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-11T10:38:26-08:00","id":309304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts?p=309251#post309251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So basically the idea of &quot;Seeming Contracts&quot; is that they are contracts that 5 of the 6 Seemings have an affinity for. If you are one of those 5, you get the basic ability of the Contract, but then you also get a bonus which is based on your seeming. You can buy the bonus of another seeming for a second dot. If you're the one Seeming not on the list, then you have to pay extra, but get to pick which seeming bonus you get from the contract.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the gist, though please stand by for pedantic nitpicking!<br /> <br /> It sounds more like each represented Seeming gets its own version, with no basic effect to be seen. Those versions have some similarities, but they definitely function differently. Also, some Seeming Contracts may have all 6 Seemings represented; he simply said most will have 5, not 6.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-11T19:47:36-08:00","id":309767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts?p=309304#post309304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's the gist, though please stand by for pedantic nitpicking!<br /> <br /> It sounds more like each represented Seeming gets its own version, with no basic effect to be seen. Those versions have some similarities, but they definitely function differently. Also, some Seeming Contracts may have all 6 Seemings represented; he simply said most will have 5, not 6.</div> </div> </div> </div>The reason for most being 5 not 6 is probably related to how some seemings are opposites. Ogre and Fairest, Beast and Wizened, they seem opposite in theme and the way they work, while Elemental and Darkling don't seem to oppose any seeming (Darkling might seem opposite to Fairest, but then there's Shadowsoul).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4261-donpapillon","name":"donpapillon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4261_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-11T19:51:14-08:00","id":309771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts?p=309304#post309304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's the gist, though please stand by for pedantic nitpicking!<br /> <br /> It sounds more like each represented Seeming gets its own version, with no basic effect to be seen. Those versions have some similarities, but they definitely function differently. Also, some Seeming Contracts may have all 6 Seemings represented; he simply said most will have 5, not 6.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, yeah, I did misremember the basic effect thing. With regarding the 5-6 seemings, I was oversimplifying for clarity, but yeah. <br /> <br /> Combine the ability to take effects outside your seeming with the disassociation of kiths and seemings, and the number of character concepts which can be created easily skyrocket.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2291-gwyn-chan-r-gwyll","name":"Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-15T22:43:25-08:00","id":313512,"title":"","content":"So I had an idea hit me for a narrative difference with Contracts.<br /> <br /> If you've read stuff of mine, you'll know I've talked about Conflict Answers before(Essentially, the answer to any conflict is essentially Yes, Yes And, Yes,But, No, No And, and No But). You've probably also heard me talk about how the system of WoD essentially reflects this, Exceptional Successes usually being Yes And answers, Successes usually being Yes answer with the occasional Yes But, Failures usually being No answers, and Dramatic Failures being No And's. The notion I'm poking is in here, but let's establish what happened with Contracts first.<br /> <br /> In 1st Edition, when you bought a Contract, what you really bought was the right to barter with a facet of reality, each clause defining just how much business you were allowed to do. From there, each evocation was the changeling doing business, paying in Glamour or with a Catch and your die roll essentially representing your metaphysical smoozing and haggling for quality of product.<br /> <br /> Now fans know already that there's a slight error of sorts with this idea, in that unless you got Exceptional Successes, the product didn't change much-you often only needed one success to get the full bang(Well, the standard product). This led to a trade off-Contracts, as a rule, were more consistent with uses but less powerful as a result.<br /> <br /> So here's what I'm thinking, as a different interpretation of that idea-readjust the idea of right to barter by establishing Failures as Yes But or No But Answers. The Idea is that a contract is consistently reliable so long as you don't egregiously offend the facet of reality(Dramatic Failure), but creates a better sense of that haggling. By buying a Contract, reality has agreed to do this for that already rather than simply agreeing to chat with you. Using a Contract usually means that something will always happen according to the deal, it's just a matter of if reality feels like cheating you a little. This puts a little bit of Goblin in every Contract.<br /> <br /> A Dramatic Failure isn't adjusted, but it's understood that the circumstances you are trying to force it to act in are a major violation of Contract-not only a No And answer, but possibly one that damages the relationship and may bar a changeling from using it until restitution is made.<br /> <br /> Just a thought.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-15T23:05:21-08:00","id":313533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts?p=244865#post244865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That would be something we'd really love to do. It could be challenging with our Court format (we're offering examples by city), but I'd really like to.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could see that book working well","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-16T02:40:04-08:00","id":313582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts?p=313512#post313512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I had an idea hit me for a narrative difference with Contracts. ( And a rest)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes And... Yes! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I'm very fond of changelings powers to be unrealiable in small way, but also generally &quot;you bargined it before, with activation you just makes details on this particular use&quot;. VERY fea like. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-27T21:27:22-07:00","id":680655,"title":"","content":"Apologies for disturbing this shade, but I'd like to add that this new system seems costly. All the Powerstats in 2ED cost 5 Experiences per dot. A power costing the same as a dot of Powerstat seems too expensive, unless they are very potent. I like this idea that you can unlock different versions of the same Contract for 1 Experience each, with one Seeming having no unique version in most cases. However, it makes the whole package seem even more expensive. This could be mitigated with a second category of Experiences that can be used alongside Regular Experiences to buy Wyrd and Contract dots, kinda like the Arcane Experiences in 2ED Mage. The new spin on Seeming, Freeholds and Courts makes me think that acquiring these Wyrd Beats would involve exploring your personal tale somehow, as an extension of that moment you defied your Keeper and defined your own fate. I know that probably sounds like too much thematic overlap, but I'm sure the developers could think of a new way to portray this process of character progression if they wanted to. I could be wrong or misled about the whole idea, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-27T21:41:04-07:00","id":680665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts?p=680655#post680655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Apologies for disturbing this shade, but I'd like to add that this new system seems costly. All the Powerstats in 2ED cost 5 Experiences per dot. A power costing the same as a dot of Powerstat seems too expensive, unless they are very potent. I like this idea that you can unlock different versions of the same Contract for 1 Experience each, with one Seeming having no unique version in most cases. However, it makes the whole package seem even more expensive.</div> </div> </div> </div>The first Facet of a non-affinity Gift in Werewolf costs five Experiences and every other Facet thereafter costs two more each.<br /> <br /> A five-dot Merit costs the same as a dot of Supernatural Tolerance; I'm somehow doubtful you have the same complaint about Psychokinesis 5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-27T21:50:02-07:00","id":680669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts?p=680665#post680665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The first Facet of a non-affinity Gift in Werewolf costs five Experiences and every other Facet thereafter costs two more each.<br /> <br /> A five-dot Merit costs the same as a dot of Supernatural Tolerance; I'm somehow doubtful you have the same complaint about Psychokinesis 5.</div> </div> </div> </div>5 Experiences, or 5 Beats?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-27T21:59:15-07:00","id":680673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts?p=680669#post680669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 5 Experiences, or 5 Beats?</div> </div> </div> </div>Literally nothing in 2e costs a number of Beats except in the sense that Experiences are made of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-28T12:06:04-07:00","id":681296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts?p=680665#post680665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The first Facet of a non-affinity Gift in Werewolf costs five Experiences and every other Facet thereafter costs two more each.<br /> <br /> A five-dot Merit costs the same as a dot of Supernatural Tolerance; I'm somehow doubtful you have the same complaint about Psychokinesis 5.</div> </div> </div> </div>The takeaway here is that it's not high-end Contracts that are significantly more expensive in 2nd edition, it's Wyd dots that are significantly cheaper.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://fo